window.EXAM_DATA = {"id":"t2","title":"Topic 2 · completo","title_es":"Topic 2 · todas las preguntas (incluye secuenciales y Case Studies del Topic)","cases":{"CS2":{"title":"Case Study: Fabrikam, Inc.","en":"<h4>Background</h4>\n<p>Fabrikam, Inc., is a manufacturer of products for the gift industry. The company plans to implement Business Central as its new enterprise resource planning (ERP) system.</p>\n<p>The company sells to two types of customers: wholesale and retail. Retail customers order at special events and online. Wholesale customers send in orders by email.</p>\n<h4>Current Environment</h4>\n<p><b>Order processing</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The company uses a purchase order (PO) workflow for any PO over $500.</li>\n<li>The system has been fully configured for sales order prepayments and will check for a prepayment invoice at posting.</li>\n<li>Customers can special order products with a prepayment that is due on receipt.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Invoicing</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Wholesale customer payment terms are net 30, with a 2% discount if paid within 10 days.</li>\n<li>Retail customer payment terms are payable on receipt or shipment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Reporting</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The company uses headcount (number of employees) and square footage for statistical accounts.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Integrations</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The company currently uses Outlook, Excel, Word, and Teams to communicate internally and externally with customers and vendors.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Requirements</h4>\n<p><b>Order processing</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The company must be able to combine multiple purchase receipts into one vendor invoice.</li>\n<li>Posted vendor invoices must be reverted when damages are reported or a product is returned to the vendor.</li>\n<li>Fully invoiced POs must not appear on the PO list page.</li>\n<li>Customer prepayments vary based on customer relationship. Special orders from new customers have a 25% prepayment. Established customers have only a 15% prepayment.</li>\n<li>The company must be able to approve POs by email without opening Business Central.</li>\n<li>Customers often reorder the same items with similar quantities. The system must be configured to ask the user if recurring lines should be added to sales orders.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Invoicing</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Customer revenue must be posted to separate general ledger (G/L) accounts based on customer type. The G/L account must have subcategories for wholesale and retail revenue.</li>\n<li>Accounts receivable must be posted to separate G/L accounts based on customer type. The G/L account must have subcategories for wholesale and retail accounts receivable.</li>\n<li>Currently, inventory is sold at a cost based on purchase and sales over a period.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Reporting</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Financial reports must include statistical accounts.</li>\n<li>The financial report structure must map to account categories.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Integrations</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Create sales orders while collaborating with customers by email.</li>\n<li>Edit customer information while messaging the sales team in a group chat.</li>\n<li>Communicate a brochure to all customers at once about a sales campaign.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>General ledger posting accounts</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Retail Receivables = 13100</li>\n<li>Wholesale Receivables = 13200</li>\n<li>Payment Discount = 54800</li>\n<li>Retail Sales = 44100</li>\n<li>Wholesale Sales = 44200</li>\n<li>Sales Prepayments = 22160</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Issues</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Order entry takes too long for wholesale customers.</li>\n<li>Vendors ship partial orders but send one monthly invoice. The company is unable to associate one invoice with multiple POs in the current environment.</li>\n<li>Inventory reconciliation was difficult in the company's old system because it allowed users to sell more inventory than was physically available.</li>\n<li>Users must log in to the system to provide workflow approvals.</li>\n</ul>","es":"<h4>Contexto</h4>\n<p>Fabrikam, Inc. fabrica productos para la industria del regalo y va a implantar Business Central como nuevo ERP.</p>\n<p>Vende a dos tipos de clientes: mayoristas (wholesale) y minoristas (retail). Los minoristas compran en eventos especiales y online; los mayoristas envían los pedidos por email.</p>\n<h4>Entorno actual</h4>\n<p><b>Procesamiento de pedidos</b></p><ul><li>Hay un workflow de pedidos de compra (PO) para cualquier PO de más de 500 $.</li><li>El sistema está configurado para anticipos (prepayments) en pedidos de venta y comprueba la factura de anticipo al registrar.</li><li>Los clientes pueden hacer pedidos especiales con un anticipo pagadero a la recepción.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Facturación</b></p><ul><li>Clientes mayoristas: neto a 30 días, con un 2 % de descuento si pagan en 10 días.</li><li>Clientes minoristas: pago a la recepción o al envío.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Informes</b></p><ul><li>Usa la plantilla (número de empleados) y los metros cuadrados como cuentas estadísticas.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Integraciones</b></p><ul><li>Usa Outlook, Excel, Word y Teams para comunicarse interna y externamente.</li></ul>\n<h4>Requisitos</h4>\n<p><b>Procesamiento de pedidos</b></p><ul><li>Debe poder combinar varias recepciones de compra en una sola factura de proveedor.</li><li>Las facturas de proveedor registradas deben revertirse si hay daños o se devuelve el producto.</li><li>Los pedidos de compra totalmente facturados no deben aparecer en la lista de pedidos.</li><li>El anticipo depende de la relación con el cliente: pedidos especiales de clientes nuevos 25 %; clientes habituales solo 15 %.</li><li>Debe poder aprobar pedidos de compra por email sin abrir Business Central.</li><li>Los clientes suelen repetir los mismos productos con cantidades parecidas: el sistema debe preguntar si añadir las líneas recurrentes a los pedidos de venta.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Facturación</b></p><ul><li>Los ingresos deben registrarse en cuentas distintas según el tipo de cliente, con subcategorías para mayorista y minorista.</li><li>Las cuentas a cobrar deben registrarse en cuentas distintas según el tipo de cliente, con subcategorías para mayorista y minorista.</li><li>Hoy el inventario se vende a un coste basado en compras y ventas de un periodo.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Informes</b></p><ul><li>Los informes financieros deben incluir cuentas estadísticas.</li><li>La estructura del informe financiero debe corresponder a las categorías de cuentas.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Integraciones</b></p><ul><li>Crear pedidos de venta mientras se colabora con clientes por email.</li><li>Editar datos de clientes mientras se chatea con el equipo de ventas en un chat de grupo.</li><li>Enviar a la vez a todos los clientes un folleto sobre una campaña de ventas.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Cuentas contables</b></p><ul><li>Retail Receivables = 13100</li><li>Wholesale Receivables = 13200</li><li>Payment Discount = 54800</li><li>Retail Sales = 44100</li><li>Wholesale Sales = 44200</li><li>Sales Prepayments = 22160</li></ul>\n<h4>Problemas</h4><ul><li>La introducción de pedidos de mayoristas es demasiado lenta.</li><li>Los proveedores envían pedidos parciales pero una sola factura mensual; hoy no se puede asociar una factura a varios pedidos.</li><li>La conciliación de inventario era difícil porque el sistema permitía vender más de lo que había físicamente.</li><li>Los usuarios deben entrar en el sistema para aprobar los workflows.</li></ul>"},"CS1":{"title":"Case Study: Northwind Traders","en":"<h4>Background</h4>\n<p>Northwind Traders is an independent, family-owned business. The company distributes natural pet products in the Northwest region of the country/region. Products are purchased directly from manufacturers and distributed by using its own fleet of trucks.</p>\n<p>When the company started, deliveries were within a three-hour radius of the warehouse. Due to regional growth, current deliveries require drivers to stay overnight on some routes. The company plans to open a second warehouse to expand the region and eliminate overnights for route drivers. The company also plans to hire a second group of employees to run operations in this new location. The finance and accounting teams will remain in the original location.</p>\n<p>The company uses a third-party system for financials and order management. The finance department stated that the company's fiscal year begins on July 1 and ends on June 30. The mm/dd/yyyy date format is used.</p>\n<p>As part of the expansion, the owner plans to upgrade to an ERP system and use Business Central to fulfill the company requirements and manage growth.</p>\n<h4>Current environment</h4>\n<p><b>Orders</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Orders are emailed to customer service and manually keyed into the inventory system.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Pricing and discounts</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Customer pricing is determined by the customer market type. Customer market types are Retail, Veterinarian, and Breeder. Each customer is associated with only one market type.</li>\n<li>Vendors offer monthly promotions to customers by item, brand, or item category.</li>\n<li>Invoices should show each customer's base price, the discount amount, and the net price.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Accounts payable</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The company wants to expand vendor payment options in the new system.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Requirements</h4>\n<p><b>Customers</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The sales team must be able to: quickly set up new customers with the proper settings based on customer type; identify customers by market type. Customer posting groups will be used to identify which market the customer belongs to.</li>\n<li>Base price is determined by the customer market type.</li>\n<li>The sales department should receive a warning when entering the order if a customer is over their credit limit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Sales</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Customer discounts are offered for specific time frames by item, brand, or product category. Discounts should be added to sales lines automatically.</li>\n<li>Discounts must post to a unique general ledger (G/L) account.</li>\n<li>The business needs to be able to track revenue by location, market, and product category dimensions. Locations 100 and 200 will be set as default dimensions on the two warehouse locations. Food, treats, toys, and supplies are the required product categories, which will be set as default dimensions on the item cards. Each customer card will have a default market dimension.</li>\n<li>The sales manager wants to delete canceled orders and automatically archive them.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Warehouse</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Orders will be fulfilled from two possible warehouse locations.</li>\n<li>Product will be transferred between locations by using transfer orders.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Sales invoices</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Invoices will be posted after delivery.</li>\n<li>Invoices will be emailed to the customer.</li>\n<li>The sales department must be able to quickly correct posted invoices for: posted invoices that have not been paid; posted invoices that have been paid; posted invoices created from sales orders; posted invoices not created from sales orders.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Accounting</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The finance department requires that the company has 12 monthly accounting periods per fiscal year.</li>\n<li>Finance department users must be able to reconcile the accounts receivable (AR) subledger to the G/L account at month end.</li>\n<li>AR department users need the ability to settle and close invoices when customers take payment discounts after the payment discount date has passed. AR users should be allowed to accept or reject the payment tolerance.</li>\n<li>Accounts payable (AP) department users must be able to pay vendors by electronic funds transfer (EFT) and use a payment journal batch named EFT to process payments.</li>\n<li>When viewing G/L entries, the finance and accounting teams must be able to see debits and credits instead of a positive or negative amount.</li>\n<li>The company needs to be able to track expenses by department and location. The departments are sales, operations, and administration.</li>\n<li>AR must be able to correct cash application entries.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Issues</h4>\n<p><b>Payment application</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Customers may have several stores that are responsible for their own orders and payments.</li>\n<li>Occasionally, AR clerks mistakenly apply payments to the incorrect customer invoice.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Invoicing</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>When items are delivered, customers refuse the items for reasons such as damaged or wrong item.</li>\n<li>After the invoices are posted, they must be corrected, which is time-consuming.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Warehouse</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The sales department and warehouse managers must have visibility into products that are in the process of being transferred between locations.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Accounts</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Customer accounts are difficult to view by market type.</li>\n<li>The finance team does not have the ability to report revenue by customer type.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Accounting</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>AR users often find variances between the AR subledger and G/L account.</li>\n<li>Customers often take the payment discount after the payment discount date has passed, leaving open invoices for small amounts.</li>\n<li>The AP department is unable to pay vendors by EFT in the current system.</li>\n<li>Finance and accounting team members have trouble validating postings when they use only the amounts field on G/L entries.</li>\n<li>The finance department is unable to run financial reports by market. All revenue postings must reference a market.</li>\n</ul>","es":"<h4>Contexto</h4>\n<p>Northwind Traders es una empresa familiar independiente que distribuye productos naturales para mascotas en la región noroeste del país. Compra directamente a los fabricantes y reparte con su propia flota de camiones.</p>\n<p>Al principio, las entregas estaban a menos de tres horas del almacén. Con el crecimiento, algunas rutas obligan a los conductores a pasar la noche fuera. La empresa va a abrir un segundo almacén para ampliar la región y evitar esas noches, y contratará otro equipo para operar en la nueva ubicación. Finanzas y contabilidad seguirán en la ubicación original.</p>\n<p>Hoy usa un sistema de terceros para finanzas y gestión de pedidos. Su ejercicio (fiscal year) empieza el 1 de julio y termina el 30 de junio. Se usa el formato de fecha mm/dd/yyyy.</p>\n<p>Con la expansión, el propietario quiere pasar a un ERP y usar Business Central.</p>\n<h4>Entorno actual</h4>\n<p><b>Pedidos</b></p><ul><li>Los pedidos llegan por email a atención al cliente y se teclean a mano en el sistema de inventario.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Precios y descuentos</b></p><ul><li>El precio depende del tipo de mercado del cliente: Retail, Veterinarian y Breeder. Cada cliente pertenece a un solo mercado.</li><li>Los proveedores ofrecen promociones mensuales por producto, marca o categoría.</li><li>Las facturas deben mostrar el precio base, el importe del descuento y el precio neto.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Cuentas a pagar</b></p><ul><li>La empresa quiere ampliar las formas de pago a proveedores en el nuevo sistema.</li></ul>\n<h4>Requisitos</h4>\n<p><b>Clientes</b></p><ul><li>El equipo de ventas debe poder dar de alta clientes rápidamente con la configuración correcta según su tipo e identificar a los clientes por mercado. Se usarán los customer posting groups para identificar el mercado de cada cliente.</li><li>El precio base depende del mercado del cliente.</li><li>Ventas debe recibir un aviso al introducir el pedido si el cliente supera su límite de crédito.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Ventas</b></p><ul><li>Los descuentos se ofrecen durante periodos concretos por producto, marca o categoría y deben añadirse automáticamente a las líneas de venta.</li><li>Los descuentos deben registrarse en una cuenta contable (G/L) propia.</li><li>Hay que analizar los ingresos por las dimensiones ubicación, mercado y categoría de producto. Las ubicaciones 100 y 200 serán default dimensions de los dos almacenes; las categorías Food, Treats, Toys y Supplies serán default dimensions en las fichas de producto; cada cliente tendrá una dimensión de mercado por defecto.</li><li>El jefe de ventas quiere borrar los pedidos cancelados y archivarlos automáticamente.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Almacén</b></p><ul><li>Los pedidos se servirán desde dos almacenes posibles.</li><li>Los productos se moverán entre almacenes con transfer orders.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Facturas de venta</b></p><ul><li>Las facturas se registrarán después de la entrega.</li><li>Se enviarán al cliente por email.</li><li>Ventas debe poder corregir rápidamente facturas registradas: no pagadas, pagadas, creadas desde pedidos de venta y no creadas desde pedidos.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Contabilidad</b></p><ul><li>Finanzas necesita 12 periodos contables mensuales por ejercicio.</li><li>Finanzas debe poder conciliar a fin de mes el subledger de clientes (AR) con la cuenta contable.</li><li>AR debe poder liquidar y cerrar facturas cuando el cliente se toma el descuento por pronto pago después de la fecha de descuento, pudiendo aceptar o rechazar la tolerancia.</li><li>Cuentas a pagar (AP) debe poder pagar por transferencia electrónica (EFT) usando una sección del diario de pagos llamada EFT.</li><li>Al ver los movimientos contables, finanzas quiere ver debe y haber en lugar de importes positivos o negativos.</li><li>Hay que analizar los gastos por departamento (ventas, operaciones, administración) y ubicación.</li><li>AR debe poder corregir aplicaciones de cobros.</li></ul>\n<h4>Problemas</h4>\n<p><b>Aplicación de pagos</b></p><ul><li>Algunos clientes tienen varias tiendas responsables de sus propios pedidos y pagos.</li><li>A veces AR aplica los pagos a la factura equivocada.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Facturación</b></p><ul><li>Al entregar, los clientes rechazan productos (dañados, equivocados…).</li><li>Después de registrar las facturas hay que corregirlas, lo que lleva mucho tiempo.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Almacén</b></p><ul><li>Ventas y los responsables de almacén deben ver los productos que se están transfiriendo entre almacenes.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Cuentas</b></p><ul><li>Es difícil ver las cuentas de clientes por mercado.</li><li>Finanzas no puede informar de los ingresos por tipo de cliente.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Contabilidad</b></p><ul><li>AR encuentra a menudo diferencias entre el subledger de clientes y la cuenta contable.</li><li>Los clientes se toman el descuento después de la fecha, dejando facturas abiertas por importes pequeños.</li><li>AP no puede pagar por EFT con el sistema actual.</li><li>Finanzas tiene problemas para validar registros usando solo el campo Amount de los G/L entries.</li><li>Finanzas no puede sacar informes por mercado. Todos los registros de ingresos deben llevar un mercado.</li></ul>"}},"questions":[{"id":"t2q1","type":"mc","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central to manage receivables.<br><br>You must import a series of payments from a bank account and automatically match the payments against similar ledger entries already entered in Business Central.<br><br>You need to import and apply the payments to the ledger entries that are automatically matched by the system.<br><br>Which form should you use?","es":"Debes importar una serie de pagos de una cuenta bancaria y emparejarlos automáticamente con los movimientos ya registrados en Business Central.<br><br>¿Qué página debes usar?","src":"Topic 2 · Q1","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Payment services","es":"Payment services"},{"id":"B","en":"Payment Application Rules","es":"Payment Application Rules"},{"id":"C","en":"Payment Reconciliation Journal","es":"Payment Reconciliation Journal (diario de conciliación de pagos)"},{"id":"D","en":"Payment Registration","es":"Payment Registration"}]},{"id":"t2q2","type":"hotspot","en":"You complete the sales invoicing process for a company.<br><br>You need to validate the setup.<br><br>Which setup should you check for each process? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Has completado el proceso de facturación de ventas de una empresa y debes validar la configuración.<br><br>¿Qué configuración debes revisar para cada proceso?","src":"Topic 2 · Q2","rowsHeader":["Process","Setup"],"rows":[{"en":"Create a shipment document for every item sale.","es":"Crear un documento de envío por cada venta de artículos.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Document Sending Profiles","es":"Document Sending Profiles"},{"id":"b","en":"General Ledger Setup","es":"General Ledger Setup"},{"id":"c","en":"No. Series","es":"No. Series"},{"id":"d","en":"Sales & Receivables Setup","es":"Sales & Receivables Setup"}]},{"en":"Store PDF files of sales invoices and credit memos automatically at the end of each day.","es":"Guardar automáticamente en PDF las facturas y abonos de venta al final de cada día.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Document Sending Profiles","es":"Document Sending Profiles"},{"id":"b","en":"General Ledger Setup","es":"General Ledger Setup"},{"id":"c","en":"Inventory Setup","es":"Inventory Setup"},{"id":"d","en":"Sales & Receivables Setup","es":"Sales & Receivables Setup"}]}]},{"id":"t2q3","type":"mc","en":"You are creating payment terms.<br><br>A company processes standard vendor payments on the seventh day of the next month.<br><br>You need to set up payment terms for the vendor.<br><br>Which date formula should you use?","es":"Estás creando payment terms (términos de pago). La empresa paga normalmente a los proveedores el día 7 del mes siguiente.<br><br>¿Qué fórmula de fecha debes usar?","src":"Topic 2 · Q3","options":[{"id":"A","en":"37D","es":"37D"},{"id":"B","en":"1M+7D","es":"1M+7D"},{"id":"C","en":"1M+6D","es":"1M+6D"},{"id":"D","en":"CM+7D","es":"CM+7D"}]},{"id":"t2q4","type":"mc","en":"A company purchases items by using cash. You register a vendor payment when you post a purchase invoice for a cash vendor.<br><br>You are creating a new cash vendor. No prior vendors have been set up as cash vendors.<br><br>You need to set up the vendor so that payments post automatically when you post a purchase invoice.<br><br>Which type of setup should you use?","es":"Una empresa compra productos al contado. Al registrar la factura de compra de un proveedor de contado, se registra también el pago.<br><br>Creas un proveedor de contado nuevo; nunca antes se ha configurado ninguno.<br><br>Debes configurarlo para que el pago se registre automáticamente al registrar la factura de compra. ¿Qué configuración debes usar?","src":"Topic 2 · Q4","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Payment Method as Cash","es":"Payment Method = Cash"},{"id":"B","en":"Payment Term as COD","es":"Payment Term = COD"},{"id":"C","en":"Payment Method as Cash with balancing account","es":"Payment Method = Cash con cuenta de contrapartida (balancing account)"},{"id":"D","en":"Prepayment","es":"Prepayment"}]},{"id":"t2q5","type":"drag","en":"You need to configure a new journal template.<br><br>What should you do? To answer, drag the appropriate fields to the correct requirements. Each field may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Debes configurar una nueva plantilla de diario (journal template).<br><br>¿Qué campo debes usar para cada requisito? Cada uno puede usarse una vez, varias o ninguna.","src":"Topic 2 · Q5","valuesTitle":"Fields","targetHeader":["Requirement","Field"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Force Doc. Balance","es":"Force Doc. Balance"},{"id":"V2","en":"Bal. Account Type and Bal. Account No.","es":"Bal. Account Type and Bal. Account No."},{"id":"V3","en":"Source Code","es":"Source Code"},{"id":"V4","en":"Reason Code","es":"Reason Code"}],"targets":[{"en":"Create journal lines that must balance by document number and document type.","es":"Las líneas deben cuadrar por número y tipo de documento."},{"en":"Create journal lines that must specify a default balancing account.","es":"Las líneas deben tener una cuenta de contrapartida por defecto."},{"en":"Create journal lines that use the origin of the entry as the basis for an audit trail.","es":"Las líneas usan el origen del asiento como base de la pista de auditoría."},{"en":"Create journal lines that must include a reason why an entry was made and can be used for the audit trail.","es":"Las líneas deben indicar el motivo del asiento, útil para la auditoría."}]},{"id":"t2q6","type":"mc","en":"Monetary amounts for local currency must always display three decimal places.<br><br>In General Ledger Setup, you need to configure the appropriate setup field with the appropriate value.<br><br>What should you do?","es":"Los importes en divisa local (LCY) deben mostrarse siempre con tres decimales.<br><br>En General Ledger Setup debes configurar el campo adecuado con el valor adecuado.<br><br>¿Qué debes hacer?","src":"Topic 2 · Q6","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Set the value of Amount Decimal Places to 3:3","es":"Poner Amount Decimal Places = 3:3"},{"id":"B","en":"Set the value of Unit-Amount Decimal Places to 3:3","es":"Poner Unit-Amount Decimal Places = 3:3"},{"id":"C","en":"Set the value of Inv. Rounding Precision to 0.001","es":"Poner Inv. Rounding Precision = 0.001"},{"id":"D","en":"Set the value of Unit-Amount Rounding Precision to 0.001","es":"Poner Unit-Amount Rounding Precision = 0.001"},{"id":"E","en":"Set the value of Amount Rounding Precision to 0.001","es":"Poner Amount Rounding Precision = 0.001"}]},{"id":"t2q7","type":"hotspot","en":"A bank is implementing Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>Each bank account must be configured to a unique G/L Account.<br><br>You need to set up the first bank account.<br><br>How should you configure the system? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Un banco implanta Business Central. Cada cuenta bancaria debe tener su propia cuenta contable.<br><br>¿Cómo debes configurar la primera cuenta bancaria?","src":"Topic 2 · Q7","rowsHeader":["Field","Assignment"],"rows":[{"en":"Bank Account Nos.","es":"Bank Account Nos. (serie numérica)","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Bank Account Posting groups","es":"Bank Account Posting groups"},{"id":"b","en":"General Ledger Setup","es":"General Ledger Setup"},{"id":"c","en":"Cash Flow Setup","es":"Cash Flow Setup"},{"id":"d","en":"Source Code Setup","es":"Source Code Setup"}]},{"en":"G/L Account for the bank account","es":"Cuenta contable de la cuenta bancaria","options":[{"id":"a","en":"General Business Posting group","es":"General Business Posting group"},{"id":"b","en":"Bank Account Posting group","es":"Bank Account Posting group"},{"id":"c","en":"General Posting Setup","es":"General Posting Setup"},{"id":"d","en":"Bank Account Currency Code","es":"Bank Account Currency Code"}]}]},{"id":"t2q8","type":"mc","en":"A company has been using Dynamics 365 Business Central for many years.<br><br>A new accounting manager for the company reviews the chart of accounts. The manager wants to remove some general ledger accounts.<br><br>The Check G/L Account Usage field is selected in the General Ledger Setup.<br><br>You need to assist with the account deletions.<br><br>What is one requirement that enables deletion of a general ledger account?","es":"Una empresa usa Business Central desde hace años. El nuevo responsable de contabilidad revisa el chart of accounts (plan de cuentas) y quiere eliminar algunas cuentas.<br><br>En General Ledger Setup está marcado <b>Check G/L Account Usage</b>.<br><br>¿Qué requisito permite eliminar una cuenta de contabilidad?","src":"Topic 2 · Q8","options":[{"id":"A","en":"The account cannot be used in any posting groups or posting setup","es":"La cuenta no puede estar usada en ningún posting group (grupo contable) ni posting setup"},{"id":"B","en":"The account cannot be used in any account schedule.","es":"La cuenta no puede estar usada en ningún account schedule (financial report)."},{"id":"C","en":"The general ledger account cannot allow for direct posting.","es":"La cuenta no puede permitir Direct Posting."},{"id":"D","en":"The account must have ledger entries.","es":"La cuenta debe tener movimientos."}]},{"id":"t2q9","type":"mc","en":"The general ledger account for accounts receivable must match the sum of all balances on the customer cards.<br><br>You need to set up the general ledger account card for accounts receivable to meet this requirement.<br><br>What should you do?","es":"La cuenta del libro mayor de clientes (cuentas a cobrar) debe coincidir con la suma de los saldos de las fichas de cliente.<br><br>Debes configurar la ficha de esa cuenta para cumplirlo. ¿Qué debes hacer?","src":"Topic 2 · Q9","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Configure the account type.","es":"Configurar el tipo de cuenta (Account Type)."},{"id":"B","en":"Block the account.","es":"Bloquear la cuenta."},{"id":"C","en":"Configure totaling.","es":"Configurar el campo Totaling."},{"id":"D","en":"Disallow direct posting.","es":"No permitir el registro directo (Direct Posting)."}]},{"id":"t2q10","type":"hotspot","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The company wants to automate sales credit memo processing.<br><br>You need to configure the system to meet the requirements.<br><br>What should you do? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Una empresa usa Business Central y quiere automatizar los abonos de venta (sales credit memos).<br><br>¿Qué debes hacer para cada requisito?","src":"Topic 2 · Q10","rowsHeader":["Requirement","Action"],"rows":[{"en":"Ensure that the costs on credit memos match the costs from the originating invoice.","es":"Que el coste de los abonos coincida con el de la factura original.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Select Exact Cost Reversing Mandatory","es":"Select Exact Cost Reversing Mandatory"},{"id":"b","en":"Choose a No.Series for Posted Credit Memo Nos.","es":"Choose a No.Series for Posted Credit Memo Nos."},{"id":"c","en":"Choose Yes to Archive Return Orders","es":"Choose Yes to Archive Return Orders"},{"id":"d","en":"Add a Sales Credit Memo Account in General Posting Setup","es":"Add a Sales Credit Memo Account in General Posting Setup"}]},{"en":"Process the receipt of a return at the same time the credit memo is posted.","es":"Registrar la recepción de la devolución al registrar el abono.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Select Return Receipt on Credit Memo","es":"Select Return Receipt on Credit Memo"},{"id":"b","en":"Select Shipment on Invoice","es":"Select Shipment on Invoice"},{"id":"c","en":"Choose Skip Manual Reservation","es":"Choose Skip Manual Reservation"},{"id":"d","en":"Choose Blank for Default Quantity to Ship","es":"Choose Blank for Default Quantity to Ship"}]},{"en":"List a default quantity of one on the credit memo lines.","es":"Proponer una cantidad de 1 en las líneas del abono.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Choose Yes for Default Item Quantity","es":"Choose Yes for Default Item Quantity"},{"id":"b","en":"Choose Remainder for Default Quantity to Ship","es":"Choose Remainder for Default Quantity to Ship"},{"id":"c","en":"Choose No for Default Item Quantity","es":"Choose No for Default Item Quantity"},{"id":"d","en":"Choose Blank for Default Quantity to Ship","es":"Choose Blank for Default Quantity to Ship"}]}]},{"id":"t2q11","type":"drag","en":"You are implementing Dynamics 365 Business Central. The accounting manager of the company provides you with the chart of accounts.<br><br>You need to set up specific posting groups according to the chart of accounts.<br><br>Which setup should you use? To answer, drag the appropriate setup to the correct action. Each setup may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Estás implantando Business Central y el responsable de contabilidad te da el plan de cuentas. Debes configurar los grupos contables específicos.<br><br>¿Qué configuración debes usar para cada acción? Cada una puede usarse una vez, varias o ninguna.","src":"Topic 2 · Q11","valuesTitle":"Setups","targetHeader":["Action","Setup"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Bank Account Posting Groups","es":"Bank Account Posting Groups"},{"id":"V2","en":"Customer Posting Groups","es":"Customer Posting Groups"},{"id":"V3","en":"Inventory Posting Groups and Inventory Posting Setup","es":"Inventory Posting Groups and Inventory Posting Setup"},{"id":"V4","en":"Vendor Posting Groups","es":"Vendor Posting Groups"},{"id":"V5","en":"General Posting Setup","es":"General Posting Setup"}],"targets":[{"en":"Automatic posting of received payment differences from customers","es":"Registro automático de las diferencias de pago de clientes"},{"en":"Automatic posting to the payables account","es":"Registro automático en la cuenta de proveedores (payables)"},{"en":"Automatic posting to different work in progress balance accounts, depending on the location","es":"Registro automático en distintas cuentas de WIP según la ubicación"}]},{"id":"t2q12","type":"mr","en":"You copy a General Posting Setup from an instance of Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>You must configure the General Posting Setup. You assign a category and subcategory to each account.<br><br>You need to complete the configuration as efficiently as possible.<br><br>What are three ways to complete the configuration? Each correct answer presents a complete solution.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Copias un General Posting Setup desde otra instancia de Business Central y debes completar su configuración; asignas categoría y subcategoría a cada cuenta.<br><br>Debes completar la configuración de la forma más eficiente. ¿Cuáles son tres formas de hacerlo?","src":"Topic 2 · Q12","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Use the Copy action to create a new General Posting Setup Card","es":"Usar la acción Copy para crear una ficha nueva de General Posting Setup."},{"id":"B","en":"Import a configuration package that contains the General Posting Setup","es":"Importar un configuration package que contenga el General Posting Setup."},{"id":"C","en":"Use the Suggest Accounts action to create all possible posting setup combinations","es":"Usar la acción Suggest Accounts para crear todas las combinaciones posibles."},{"id":"D","en":"Create a new General Posting Setup Card, and then use the Suggest Accounts action","es":"Crear una ficha nueva de General Posting Setup y después usar Suggest Accounts."},{"id":"E","en":"Create a new General Posting Setup Card, and then use the Copy action","es":"Crear una ficha nueva de General Posting Setup y después usar la acción Copy."}],"select":3},{"id":"t2q13","type":"hotspot","en":"A company is implementing Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The accountant must be able to report discounts received on purchased items separately from costs.<br><br>You need to configure the system to meet the requirement.<br><br>How should you configure the system? To answer, select the appropriate configurations in the answer area.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Una empresa implanta Business Central. El contable debe poder informar de los descuentos obtenidos en artículos comprados por separado del coste.<br><br>¿Cómo debes configurar el sistema?","src":"Topic 2 · Q13","rowsHeader":["Area","Configuration"],"rows":[{"en":"Purchase & Payables Setup","es":"Purchase & Payables Setup","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Invoice Discounts for Discount Posting","es":"Invoice Discounts for Discount Posting"},{"id":"b","en":"Adjust for Payment Disc.","es":"Adjust for Payment Disc."},{"id":"c","en":"Line Discounts for Discount Posting","es":"Line Discounts for Discount Posting"},{"id":"d","en":"Calc. Inv. Discount","es":"Calc. Inv. Discount"}]},{"en":"General Posting Setup","es":"General Posting Setup","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Purch. Account","es":"Purch. Account"},{"id":"b","en":"Purch. Inv. Disc. Account","es":"Purch. Inv. Disc. Account"},{"id":"c","en":"Purch. Line Disc. Account","es":"Purch. Line Disc. Account"},{"id":"d","en":"Purchase Variance Account","es":"Purchase Variance Account"}]}]},{"id":"t2q14","type":"mr","en":"A company is implementing Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The company needs to post monthly general journal batches for purchase expenses incurred throughout the month. The posted entries must have unique, incremental document numbers. The numbers must increment by one and be sequential.<br><br>You need to configure the system to meet the requirements.<br><br>Which three actions should you perform in sequence? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.","es":"Una empresa debe registrar cada mes secciones (batches) del General Journal con gastos de compra. Los movimientos registrados deben tener números de documento únicos, correlativos y que aumenten de uno en uno.<br><br>¿Qué tres acciones debes realizar?","src":"Topic 2 · Q14","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Create a Template Batch with Posting No. Series.","es":"Crear una sección (batch) con Posting No. Series."},{"id":"B","en":"Create the No. Series.","es":"Crear la No. Series."},{"id":"C","en":"Configure a General Journal with Purchase Reason Code.","es":"Configurar un General Journal con Reason Code de compras."},{"id":"D","en":"Configure a General Journal Template with Purchase Type.","es":"Configurar una plantilla General Journal Template de tipo Purchases."},{"id":"E","en":"Create a Template Batch with No. Series.","es":"Crear una sección (batch) con No. Series."}],"select":3},{"id":"t2q16","type":"drag","en":"You set up a new company for a customer. The customer provides you with the chart of accounts and the preferred grouping of items, vendors, and customers.<br><br>You must ensure that item posting corresponds with the grouping preferences and chart of accounts for the customer.<br><br>You need to create the posting groups and setup.<br><br>Which type of posting groups should you create? To answer, drag the appropriate posting group types to the correct entities. Each posting group type may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Configuras una company nueva. El cliente te da el plan de cuentas y cómo quiere agrupar artículos, proveedores y clientes.<br><br>¿Qué tipo de grupo contable corresponde a cada entidad? Cada tipo puede usarse una vez, varias o ninguna.","src":"Topic 2 · Q16","valuesTitle":"Posting group types","targetHeader":["Entity","Posting group type"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Specific posting groups","es":"Specific posting groups"},{"id":"V2","en":"General posting groups","es":"General posting groups"}],"targets":[{"en":"Sales","es":"Ventas"},{"en":"Cost of goods sold","es":"Coste de las ventas"},{"en":"Customer receivables","es":"Cuentas a cobrar de clientes"},{"en":"Vendor payables","es":"Cuentas a pagar a proveedores"}]},{"id":"t2q17","type":"hotspot","en":"You are implementing Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>You are creating an expense account for office supplies in the chart of accounts. The account may be used for purchase invoice transactions as well as general journal transactions.<br><br>You need to configure the remaining options for the account.<br><br>Which values should you use? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Estás creando en el plan de cuentas una cuenta de gastos de material de oficina, que se usará en facturas de compra y en diarios generales.<br><br>¿Qué valor debes usar en cada opción?","src":"Topic 2 · Q17","rowsHeader":["Account option","Value"],"rows":[{"en":"Account Category","es":"Account Category","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Expense","es":"Expense"},{"id":"b","en":"Cost of Goods Sold","es":"Cost of Goods Sold"},{"id":"c","en":"Income","es":"Income"},{"id":"d","en":"Liabilities","es":"Liabilities"}]},{"en":"Income / Balance","es":"Income / Balance","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Balance Sheet","es":"Balance Sheet"},{"id":"b","en":"Income Statement","es":"Income Statement"}]},{"en":"Direct Posting","es":"Direct Posting","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Yes","es":"Yes"},{"id":"b","en":"No","es":"No"}]}]},{"id":"t2q18","type":"hotspot","en":"You are implementing Dynamics 365 Business Central for a customer. The local currency code (LCY) for the company is set to US dollars ($).<br><br>The customer plans to set up a bank account. The customer provides the following information for the account:<br><br>Account number -<ul><li>Name</li><li>Address</li><li>Bank account posting group</li></ul>The account must meet the following requirements:<ul><li>Use US dollars.</li><li>Use 9075 as the number of the next bank account statement for reconciliation in Business Central.</li></ul>You need to set up the account for the customer.<br><br>Which values should you use? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"La divisa local (LCY) de la company es el dólar estadounidense. El cliente quiere crear una cuenta bancaria que:<ul><li>Use dólares estadounidenses.</li><li>Use 9075 como número del siguiente extracto para la conciliación.</li></ul>¿Qué valores debes usar?","src":"Topic 2 · Q18","rowsHeader":["Field","Value"],"rows":[{"en":"Currency Code","es":"Currency Code","options":[{"id":"a","en":"<blank>","es":"<en blanco>"},{"id":"b","en":"USD","es":"USD"},{"id":"c","en":"$","es":"$"}]},{"en":"Last Statement No.","es":"Last Statement No.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"9074","es":"9074"},{"id":"b","en":"9075","es":"9075"}]}]},{"id":"t2q19","type":"mc","en":"You are setting up Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>You need to define the Direct Cost Applied account.<br><br>Where should you define the accounts for Direct Cost Applied?","es":"Estás configurando Business Central y debes definir la cuenta Direct Cost Applied (coste directo aplicado).<br><br>¿Dónde se definen estas cuentas?","src":"Topic 2 · Q19","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Item Cards","es":"Item Cards (fichas de producto)"},{"id":"B","en":"Inventory Posting Setup","es":"Inventory Posting Setup"},{"id":"C","en":"General Posting Setups","es":"General Posting Setup"},{"id":"D","en":"Vendor Posting Groups","es":"Vendor Posting Groups"}]},{"id":"t2q20","type":"mc","en":"A company plans to verify that purchase invoices use agreed-upon prices and discounts.<br><br>The company is configuring settings on a vendor card. The company receives a validation error when creating a purchase order for the vendor.<br><br>You need to find out which setting is causing the validation error.<br><br>Which configuration option on the vendor card must you populate?","es":"Una empresa quiere comprobar que las facturas de compra usan los precios y descuentos acordados. Al configurar la ficha de un proveedor, recibe un error de validación al crear un pedido de compra para él.<br><br>¿Qué campo de la ficha del proveedor debes rellenar?","src":"Topic 2 · Q20","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Order address","es":"Order address"},{"id":"B","en":"Location code","es":"Location code"},{"id":"C","en":"Vendor Template","es":"Vendor Template"},{"id":"D","en":"Purchase Prices","es":"Purchase Prices"},{"id":"E","en":"Vendor Posting Group","es":"Vendor Posting Group"}]},{"id":"t2q21","type":"drag","en":"You are setting up the general journals and batches for an accounting department.<br><br>The accounting department has multiple users who will work simultaneously within different general journals.<br><br>You need to set up the different journal templates and batches for each user according to the company's requirements.<br><br>Which options should you use? To answer, drag the appropriate options to the correct requirements. Each option may be used once, more than once, or not at all.<br><br>You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Configuras diarios generales y secciones para un departamento contable con varios usuarios trabajando a la vez.<br><br>¿Qué opción debes usar para cada requisito? Cada una puede usarse una vez, varias o ninguna.","src":"Topic 2 · Q21","valuesTitle":"Options","targetHeader":["Requirement","Option"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Force Doc. Balance","es":"Force Doc. Balance"},{"id":"V2","en":"No. Series","es":"No. Series"},{"id":"V3","en":"Posting No. Series","es":"Posting No. Series"},{"id":"V4","en":"Standard Journal Code","es":"Standard Journal Code"},{"id":"V5","en":"Suggest Balancing Amount","es":"Suggest Balancing Amount"}],"targets":[{"en":"Prefill the amount on journal lines based on the document number.","es":"Rellenar el importe de las líneas según el número de documento."},{"en":"Assign document numbers to ledger entries independently from the user's journal batch.","es":"Asignar números de documento a los movimientos con independencia de la sección del usuario."},{"en":"Balance the journal lines by document type.","es":"Cuadrar las líneas por tipo de documento."}]},{"id":"t2q22","type":"drag","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>You need to configure payment terms with the correct due date calculation formula.<br><br>What should you do? To answer, drag the appropriate values to the correct requirements. Each value may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Una empresa usa Business Central y debes configurar términos de pago con la fórmula de vencimiento correcta.<br><br>¿Qué valor corresponde a cada requisito? Cada uno puede usarse una vez, varias o ninguna.","src":"Topic 2 · Q22","valuesTitle":"Values","targetHeader":["Due Date Calculation","Value"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"D10","es":"D10"},{"id":"V2","en":"10D","es":"10D"},{"id":"V3","en":"1M+10D","es":"1M+10D"}],"targets":[{"en":"10 days from today","es":"10 días desde hoy"},{"en":"The next 10th day of the next month","es":"El próximo día 10 del mes"},{"en":"One month + 10 days","es":"Un mes + 10 días"}]},{"id":"t2q23","type":"mr","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central for their receivables.<br><br>The company wants to mark any automatically matched payments to open invoices as not requiring a review if they match the highest degree of confidence that the two transactions are a match.<br><br>You need to configure payment matching rules.<br><br>Which three criteria should you configure? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"La empresa quiere que los pagos emparejados automáticamente con facturas abiertas con el máximo nivel de confianza se marquen como \"no requieren revisión\".<br><br>Debes configurar las reglas de emparejamiento. ¿Qué tres criterios debes configurar?","src":"Topic 2 · Q23","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Statement amount","es":"Statement amount (importe del extracto)"},{"id":"B","en":"Account number","es":"Account number (número de cuenta)"},{"id":"C","en":"Related-party fields","es":"Related-party fields (datos del tercero)"},{"id":"D","en":"Transaction date","es":"Transaction date (fecha de la transacción)"},{"id":"E","en":"Transaction text","es":"Transaction text (texto de la transacción)"}],"select":3},{"id":"t2q24","type":"drag","en":"You are implementing Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The accounting manager for the company provides you with a chart of accounts.<br><br>You need to set up the general ledger accounts correctly.<br><br>Which setups should you use? To answer, drag the appropriate setups to the correct requirements. Each setup may be used once, more than once, or not at all.<br><br>You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Estás implantando Business Central y el responsable de contabilidad te da el plan de cuentas. Debes configurar correctamente las cuentas de mayor.<br><br>¿Qué configuración debes usar para cada requisito? Cada una puede usarse una vez, varias o ninguna.","src":"Topic 2 · Q24","valuesTitle":"Setups","targetHeader":["Requirement","Setup"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Account Category and Account Subcategory","es":"Account Category and Account Subcategory"},{"id":"V2","en":"Account Type","es":"Account Type"},{"id":"V3","en":"Direct Posting","es":"Direct Posting"},{"id":"V4","en":"Income/Balance","es":"Income/Balance"}],"targets":[{"en":"The balance on the general ledger account for inventory must match the sum of all value entries on the item cards.","es":"El saldo de la cuenta de inventario debe coincidir con la suma de los value entries de los artículos."},{"en":"The general ledger account must be reported on one of the Financial Statements reports.","es":"La cuenta debe aparecer en uno de los estados financieros."},{"en":"The general ledger account must summarize the balance of other general ledger accounts.","es":"La cuenta debe totalizar el saldo de otras cuentas."},{"en":"The general ledger account must be closed during year-end closing procedures.","es":"La cuenta debe cerrarse en el cierre del ejercicio."}]},{"id":"t2q25","type":"mc","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>Which field is used to calculate the Due Date based on the Payment Terms?","es":"Una empresa usa Business Central. ¿Qué campo se usa para calcular la fecha de vencimiento (Due Date) a partir de los términos de pago (Payment Terms)?","src":"Topic 2 · Q25","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Order Date","es":"Order Date"},{"id":"B","en":"Due Date","es":"Due Date"},{"id":"C","en":"Posting Date","es":"Posting Date"},{"id":"D","en":"Document Date","es":"Document Date"}]},{"id":"t2q26","type":"mc","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central. All activity in the system is based on the company's local currency.<br><br>Sales invoice amounts must be rounded to the nearest interval based on amount.<br><br>You need to complete the configuration.<br><br>Where should you configure the setup?","es":"Una empresa usa Business Central y toda su actividad es en moneda local. Los importes de las facturas de venta deben redondearse al intervalo más próximo.<br><br>¿Dónde debes configurarlo?","src":"Topic 2 · Q26","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Currency Card","es":"Currency Card"},{"id":"B","en":"General Ledger Setup","es":"General Ledger Setup"},{"id":"C","en":"Sales &amp; Receivable Setup","es":"Sales & Receivables Setup"},{"id":"D","en":"Currency Exchange Rates","es":"Currency Exchange Rates"}]},{"id":"t2q27","type":"mc","en":"A company has been using Dynamics 365 Business Central for many years.<br><br>A new accounting manager for the company reviews the chart of accounts. The manager wants to remove some general ledger accounts.<br><br>The Check G/L Account Usage field is selected in the General Ledger Setup.<br><br>You need to assist with the account deletions.<br><br>What is one requirement that enables deletion of a general ledger account?","es":"Una empresa lleva muchos años con Business Central. El nuevo responsable de contabilidad revisa el plan de cuentas y quiere eliminar algunas cuentas. En General Ledger Setup está marcado <b>Check G/L Account Usage</b>.<br><br>¿Qué requisito permite eliminar una cuenta del libro mayor?","src":"Topic 2 · Q27","options":[{"id":"A","en":"The account cannot have a balance amount.","es":"La cuenta no puede tener saldo."},{"id":"B","en":"The account cannot be used in any account schedule.","es":"La cuenta no puede usarse en ningún account schedule."},{"id":"C","en":"The general ledger account is configured to allow for deletion","es":"La cuenta está configurada para permitir su eliminación."},{"id":"D","en":"The account must have ledger entries.","es":"La cuenta debe tener movimientos."}]},{"id":"t2q28","type":"mr","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central. You manage customer master data for the company.<br><br>You need to create new customers.<br><br>What are three possible ways to achieve the goal? Each correct answer presents a complete solution.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Una empresa usa Business Central y tú gestionas los datos maestros de clientes. Debes crear clientes nuevos.<br><br>¿Cuáles son tres formas posibles de hacerlo?","src":"Topic 2 · Q28","options":[{"id":"A","en":"On the Contacts page, select Related Information and then select Customer.","es":"En la página Contacts, seleccionar Related Information y después Customer."},{"id":"B","en":"On the Contacts page, select Create as Customer.","es":"En la página Contacts, seleccionar Create as Customer."},{"id":"C","en":"On the Configuration Template Header for the customer table, select Create Instance.","es":"En el Configuration Template Header de la tabla de clientes, seleccionar Create Instance."},{"id":"D","en":"On the Customers page, select New.","es":"En la página Customers, seleccionar New."},{"id":"E","en":"On the Customer card, select Apply Template.","es":"En la ficha del cliente, seleccionar Apply Template."}],"select":3},{"id":"t2q29","type":"mc","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>You must create a general ledger account and define the general ledger account as a purchase account for general journal transactions.<br><br>You need to configure the system.","es":"Una empresa usa Business Central. Debes crear una cuenta contable y definirla como cuenta de compras para las transacciones de diario general.<br><br>¿Qué debes hacer?","src":"Topic 2 · Q29","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Select Purchase as the value for the Gen. Posting Type field.","es":"Seleccionar Purchase en el campo Gen. Posting Type."},{"id":"B","en":"Assign a general product posting group that is linked to a purchase account.","es":"Asignar un general product posting group vinculado a una cuenta de compras."},{"id":"C","en":"Link combination of the general business posting group and general product posting group to a purchase account.","es":"Vincular la combinación de general business y product posting group a una cuenta de compras."},{"id":"D","en":"Assign a general business posting group that is linked to a purchase account.","es":"Asignar un general business posting group vinculado a una cuenta de compras."}]},{"id":"t2q30","type":"drag","en":"You are setting up new customers and items in Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>You need to configure the system.<br><br>Which posting group should you use? To answer, drag the appropriate posting groups to the correct use cases. Each posting group may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Estás dando de alta clientes y artículos nuevos en Business Central.<br><br>¿Qué grupo contable corresponde a cada caso? Cada uno puede usarse una vez, varias o ninguna.","src":"Topic 2 · Q30","valuesTitle":"Posting groups","targetHeader":["Requirement","Posting group"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Gen. Bus.","es":"Gen. Bus."},{"id":"V2","en":"Gen. Prod.","es":"Gen. Prod."},{"id":"V3","en":"Customer","es":"Customer"},{"id":"V4","en":"Inventory","es":"Inventory"}],"targets":[{"en":"Identify income statement accounts used for customer transactions.","es":"Identificar las cuentas de resultados de las operaciones con clientes."},{"en":"Identify balance sheet accounts used for customer transactions.","es":"Identificar las cuentas de balance de las operaciones con clientes."},{"en":"Identify income statement accounts used for item transactions.","es":"Identificar las cuentas de resultados de las operaciones con artículos."},{"en":"Identify balance sheet accounts used for item transactions.","es":"Identificar las cuentas de balance de las operaciones con artículos."}]},{"id":"t2q31","type":"mr","en":"A company implements Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>You need to create a new payment terms record to meet the following requirements:<ul><li>Ensure that the due date for all vendor invoices is 30 days.</li><li>Grant vendors a two percent discount if an invoice is paid within 10 days.</li></ul>Which three actions should you perform? Each correct answer presents a part of the solution<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Una empresa implanta Business Central. Debes crear unos términos de pago que cumplan:<ul><li>Vencimiento de todas las facturas de proveedor a 30 días.</li><li>Descuento del 2 % si la factura se paga en 10 días.</li></ul>¿Qué tres acciones debes realizar?","src":"Topic 2 · Q31","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Set the value of the Discount Date Calculation field to 2D.","es":"Discount Date Calculation = 2D."},{"id":"B","en":"Set the value of the Discount Date Calculation field to 10D.","es":"Discount Date Calculation = 10D."},{"id":"C","en":"Set the value of the Discount % field to 2.","es":"Discount % = 2."},{"id":"D","en":"Set the value of the Due Date Calculation field to 30D.","es":"Due Date Calculation = 30D."},{"id":"E","en":"Set the value of the Discount % field to 10.","es":"Discount % = 10."}],"select":3},{"id":"t2q32","type":"mc","en":"A company is implementing Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>Vendor open balances need to be posted to the general ledger (G/L) account directly by using the general journal.<br><br>You need to configure the G/L account to allow users to post vendor open balances to payables accounts.<br><br>Which setting should you use?","es":"Una empresa implanta Business Central. Los saldos abiertos de proveedores deben registrarse directamente en la cuenta contable usando el General Journal.<br><br>Debes configurar la cuenta para que los usuarios puedan registrar los saldos de proveedores en la cuenta de proveedores. ¿Qué campo debes usar?","src":"Topic 2 · Q32","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Account Category","es":"Account Category"},{"id":"B","en":"Income/Balance","es":"Income/Balance"},{"id":"C","en":"Default Deferral template","es":"Default Deferral template"},{"id":"D","en":"Direct Posting","es":"Direct Posting"}]},{"id":"t2q33","type":"mc","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>A user posts a Sales Invoice document that has an incorrect dimension value.<br><br>You need to update general ledger entries with the correct dimension value without inserting new ledger entries.<br><br>Which option should you use?","es":"Un usuario registra una factura de venta con un valor de dimensión incorrecto.<br><br>Debes actualizar los movimientos de contabilidad con el valor correcto sin crear movimientos nuevos. ¿Qué opción debes usar?","src":"Topic 2 · Q33","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Correct Dimensions","es":"Correct Dimensions"},{"id":"B","en":"Edit List","es":"Edit List"},{"id":"C","en":"Edit In Excel","es":"Edit in Excel"},{"id":"D","en":"Reverse Transaction","es":"Reverse Transaction"}]},{"id":"t2q35","type":"hotspot","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central. You are recording incoming payments from customers.<br><br>You must record a payment of $500 for customer 2030 with a posting date of November 16, 2022. The payment must be recorded against bank account No. 1010 with general ledger (G/L) account No. 10100.<br><br>You need to populate the cash receipt journal batch in Business Central to properly record the incoming payment to a bank account.<br><br>Which value should you use? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area,<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Registras cobros de clientes. Debes registrar un cobro de 500 $ del cliente 2030 con fecha 16/11/2022 contra la cuenta bancaria 1010 (cuenta contable 10100).<br><br>¿Qué valor debes usar en cada campo del diario de cobros?","src":"Topic 2 · Q35","rowsHeader":["Cash receipt journal field","Value"],"rows":[{"en":"Account Type","es":"Account Type","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Customer","es":"Customer"},{"id":"b","en":"G/L account","es":"G/L account"},{"id":"c","en":"Bank account","es":"Bank account"}]},{"en":"Account No.","es":"Account No.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"2030","es":"2030"},{"id":"b","en":"1010","es":"1010"}]},{"en":"Amount","es":"Amount","options":[{"id":"a","en":"$500","es":"$500"},{"id":"b","en":"-$500","es":"-$500"}]},{"en":"Bal. Account Type","es":"Bal. Account Type","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Customer","es":"Customer"},{"id":"b","en":"G/L account","es":"G/L account"},{"id":"c","en":"Bank account","es":"Bank account"}]},{"en":"Bal. Account No.","es":"Bal. Account No.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"2030","es":"2030"},{"id":"b","en":"1010","es":"1010"},{"id":"c","en":"10100","es":"10100"}]}]},{"id":"t2q36","type":"mr","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>An accountant must post sales services in a journal by using a predefined alphanumeric sequence. The accountant is using multiple general journal batches.<br><br>You need to configure invoice numbers for the journal.<br><br>Which two fields should you populate? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Un contable debe registrar servicios de venta en un diario con una secuencia alfanumérica predefinida y usa varias general journal batches (secciones del diario).<br><br>Debes configurar los números de factura del diario. ¿Qué dos campos debes rellenar?","src":"Topic 2 · Q36","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Posting No. Series field in General Journal Templates","es":"Campo Posting No. Series en General Journal Templates"},{"id":"B","en":"No. Series field in General Journal Batches","es":"Campo No. Series en General Journal Batches"},{"id":"C","en":"No. Series field in General Journal Templates","es":"Campo No. Series en General Journal Templates"},{"id":"D","en":"Posting No. Series field in General Journal Batches","es":"Campo Posting No. Series en General Journal Batches"}],"select":2},{"id":"t2q37","type":"mc","en":"You are configuring Dynamics 365 Business Central for a client.<br><br>Invoice amounts in the local currency code must be rounded to hundredths.<br><br>You need to configure the Inv. Rounding Precision (LCY) field in General Ledger Setup.<br><br>Which value should you use?","es":"Configuras Business Central para un cliente. Los importes de las facturas en moneda local deben redondearse a centésimas.<br><br>¿Qué valor debes usar en el campo <b>Inv. Rounding Precision (LCY)</b> de General Ledger Setup?","src":"Topic 2 · Q37","options":[{"id":"A","en":"0.01","es":"0.01"},{"id":"B","en":"0.20","es":"0.20"},{"id":"C","en":"1.00","es":"1.00"},{"id":"D","en":"1.11","es":"1.11"},{"id":"E","en":"2.00","es":"2.00"}]},{"id":"t2q39","type":"hotspot","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central. You are creating a general ledger (G/L) for a checking account in the chart of accounts.<br><br>You need to populate the fields on the G/L account card.<br><br>Which value should you select? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Estás creando en el plan de cuentas una cuenta de mayor para una cuenta corriente bancaria.<br><br>¿Qué valor debes seleccionar en cada campo de la ficha?","src":"Topic 2 · Q39","rowsHeader":["Field","Value"],"rows":[{"en":"Income/Balance","es":"Income/Balance","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Income statement","es":"Income statement"},{"id":"b","en":"Balance sheet","es":"Balance sheet"}]},{"en":"Account Category","es":"Account Category","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Assets","es":"Assets"},{"id":"b","en":"Liabilities","es":"Liabilities"},{"id":"c","en":"Equity","es":"Equity"},{"id":"d","en":"Income","es":"Income"},{"id":"e","en":"Expense","es":"Expense"}]},{"en":"Account Type","es":"Account Type","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Posting","es":"Posting"},{"id":"b","en":"Heading","es":"Heading"},{"id":"c","en":"Begin-Total","es":"Begin-Total"},{"id":"d","en":"End-Total","es":"End-Total"}]},{"en":"Direct Posting","es":"Direct Posting","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Enabled","es":"Enabled"},{"id":"b","en":"Disabled","es":"Disabled"}]}]},{"id":"t2q40","type":"mc","en":"A company based in the United States uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>A customer agrees to buy raw materials in the MXN (Mexican Peso) currency.<br><br>You need to set up the currency and exchange rates for this purchase.<br><br>What should you do?","es":"Una empresa de EE. UU. usa Business Central. Un cliente acepta comprar materias primas en MXN (peso mexicano).<br><br>Debes configurar la divisa y los tipos de cambio. ¿Qué debes hacer?","src":"Topic 2 · Q40","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Do not configure the currency MXN and recalculate all entries in USD before posting.","es":"No configurar la divisa MXN y recalcular todo en USD antes de registrar."},{"id":"B","en":"Configure the currency MXN, then set up the Currency Exchange Rate Service to upload currency rates automatically.","es":"Configurar la divisa MXN y después el Currency Exchange Rate Service para cargar los tipos de cambio automáticamente."},{"id":"C","en":"Use the currency MXN as a local currency in the system, then set the exchange rates manually before posting.","es":"Usar MXN como divisa local y fijar los tipos de cambio a mano antes de registrar."},{"id":"D","en":"Use the currency MXN as an additional reporting currency, then set up the Currency Exchange Rate Service to upload rates automatically.","es":"Usar MXN como additional reporting currency y configurar el Currency Exchange Rate Service."}]},{"id":"t2q41","type":"mc","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central. The company has a customer that will also be a vendor for the company in the next financial year.<br><br>The company plans to consolidate the customer and vendor balances to reduce unnecessary payments on receipts and reduce the amount of transaction fees.<br><br>You need to configure the contact card.<br><br>Which option should you configure first?","es":"Una empresa usa Business Central. Un cliente va a ser también proveedor de la empresa el próximo ejercicio.<br><br>La empresa quiere compensar los saldos de cliente y proveedor para reducir pagos y comisiones.<br><br>Debes configurar la ficha de contacto. ¿Qué opción debes configurar primero?","src":"Topic 2 · Q41","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Create as Employee","es":"Create as Employee"},{"id":"B","en":"Create as Customer","es":"Create as Customer"},{"id":"C","en":"Create as Bank","es":"Create as Bank"},{"id":"D","en":"Create as Vendor","es":"Create as Vendor"}]},{"id":"t2q42","type":"mr","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>A finance manager needs to import a bank statement CSV file into Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>You need to configure the system for the file import.<br><br>Which three pages should you use to complete the configuration? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"El responsable financiero necesita importar en Business Central un extracto bancario (bank statement) en CSV.<br><br>¿Qué tres páginas debes usar para configurar la importación?","src":"Topic 2 · Q42","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Payment Reconciliation Journal","es":"Payment Reconciliation Journal"},{"id":"B","en":"Bank Account Card","es":"Bank Account Card (ficha de banco)"},{"id":"C","en":"Bank Export/Import Setup","es":"Bank Export/Import Setup"},{"id":"D","en":"Data Exchange Definition","es":"Data Exchange Definition"},{"id":"E","en":"Report Selection - Bank Account","es":"Report Selection - Bank Account"}],"select":3},{"id":"t2q47","type":"mc","en":"A company has been using Dynamics 365 Business Central for many years.<br><br>A new accounting manager for the company reviews the chart of accounts. The manager wants to remove some general ledger accounts.<br><br>The Check G/L Account Usage field is selected in the General Ledger Setup.<br><br>You need to assist with the account deletions.<br><br>What is one requirement that enables deletion of a general ledger account?","es":"Una empresa lleva muchos años con Business Central. El nuevo responsable de contabilidad quiere eliminar algunas cuentas. En General Ledger Setup está marcado <b>Check G/L Account Usage</b>.<br><br>¿Qué requisito permite eliminar una cuenta del libro mayor?","src":"Topic 2 · Q47","options":[{"id":"A","en":"The account cannot be used in any posting groups or posting setup.","es":"La cuenta no puede usarse en ningún posting group ni posting setup."},{"id":"B","en":"The general ledger account is configured to allow for deletion.","es":"La cuenta está configurada para permitir su eliminación."},{"id":"C","en":"The general ledger account cannot allow for direct posting.","es":"La cuenta no puede permitir el registro directo."},{"id":"D","en":"The general ledger account must be of the type Balance Sheet.","es":"La cuenta debe ser de tipo Balance Sheet."}]},{"id":"t2q50","type":"mr","en":"A manufacturer is implementing Dynamics 365 Business Central as a new financial system.<br><br>The manufacturer requires financial reports to match reports produced by the current financial system.<br><br>You need to create account categories and subcategories to align with historical financial reports.<br><br>What are two possible ways to achieve this goal? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Un fabricante implanta Business Central como nuevo sistema financiero y necesita que los informes financieros coincidan con los de su sistema actual.<br><br>Debes crear categorías y subcategorías de cuentas que reflejen los informes históricos. ¿Cuáles son dos formas posibles de conseguirlo?","src":"Topic 2 · Q50","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Rename top-level account categories.","es":"Renombrar las categorías de nivel superior."},{"id":"B","en":"Create or delete account subcategories.","es":"Crear o eliminar subcategorías."},{"id":"C","en":"Create top-level account categories.","es":"Crear categorías de nivel superior."},{"id":"D","en":"Add a subcategory to the general ledger account and update the equivalent account schedule.","es":"Añadir una subcategoría a la cuenta y actualizar el account schedule equivalente."}],"select":2},{"id":"t2q51","type":"mc","en":"A company has been using Dynamics 365 Business Central for many years.<br><br>A new accounting manager for the company reviews the chart of accounts. The manager wants to remove some general ledger accounts.<br><br>The Check G/L Account Usage field is selected in the General Ledger Setup.<br><br>You need to assist with the account deletions.<br><br>What is one requirement that enables deletion of a general ledger account?","es":"Una empresa lleva muchos años con Business Central. El nuevo responsable de contabilidad quiere eliminar algunas cuentas. En General Ledger Setup está marcado <b>Check G/L Account Usage</b>.<br><br>¿Qué requisito permite eliminar una cuenta del libro mayor?","src":"Topic 2 · Q51","options":[{"id":"A","en":"The account cannot be used in any account schedule.","es":"La cuenta no puede usarse en ningún account schedule."},{"id":"B","en":"The fiscal year needs to be closed.","es":"El ejercicio debe estar cerrado."},{"id":"C","en":"The account cannot have a balance amount.","es":"La cuenta no puede tener saldo."},{"id":"D","en":"The account must have ledger entries.","es":"La cuenta debe tener movimientos."}]},{"id":"t2q52","type":"mc","en":"A company has been using Dynamics 365 Business Central for many years.<br><br>A new accounting manager for the company reviews the chart of accounts. The manager wants to remove some general ledger accounts.<br><br>The Check G/L Account Usage field is selected in the General Ledger Setup.<br><br>You need to assist with the account deletions.<br><br>What is one requirement that enables deletion of a general ledger account?","es":"Una empresa lleva muchos años con Business Central. El nuevo responsable de contabilidad quiere eliminar algunas cuentas. En General Ledger Setup está marcado <b>Check G/L Account Usage</b>.<br><br>¿Qué requisito permite eliminar una cuenta del libro mayor?","src":"Topic 2 · Q52","options":[{"id":"A","en":"The general ledger account cannot allow for direct posting.","es":"La cuenta no puede permitir el registro directo."},{"id":"B","en":"The general ledger account must be of the type Balance Sheet.","es":"La cuenta debe ser de tipo Balance Sheet."},{"id":"C","en":"The fiscal year needs to be closed.","es":"El ejercicio debe estar cerrado."},{"id":"D","en":"The account cannot be used in any posting groups or posting setup.","es":"La cuenta no puede usarse en ningún posting group ni posting setup."}]},{"id":"t2q53","type":"drag","en":"You are implementing Business Central for a company.<br><br>The company requires set up of the following postings:<ul><li>Automatic posting invoice rounding accounts for acquisition external parties</li><li>Automatic posting entries linked to activities with financial institutions</li><li>Automatic posting discounts granted to entities purchasing goods or services</li></ul>The accounting manager provides you with the chart of accounts.<br><br>Which posting group should you use for each requirement? To answer, move the appropriate posting groups to the correct requirements. Each posting group may be used once, more than once, or not at all.","es":"Implantas Business Central y la empresa necesita registrar automáticamente:<ul><li>Las cuentas de redondeo de facturas de compra a terceros.</li><li>Los movimientos ligados a operaciones con entidades financieras.</li><li>Los descuentos concedidos a quienes compran bienes o servicios.</li></ul>El responsable de contabilidad te da el plan de cuentas. ¿Qué grupo contable debes usar para cada requisito?","src":"Topic 2 · Q53","valuesTitle":"Posting groups","targetHeader":["Requirement","Posting group"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Vendor posting groups","es":"Vendor posting groups"},{"id":"V2","en":"General posting groups","es":"General posting groups"},{"id":"V3","en":"Customer posting groups","es":"Customer posting groups"},{"id":"V4","en":"Bank account posting groups","es":"Bank account posting groups"}],"targets":[{"en":"Automatic posting invoice rounding accounts for acquisition external parties","es":"Redondeo de facturas de compra a terceros"},{"en":"Automatic posting entries linked to transactional activities with financial institutions","es":"Movimientos con entidades financieras"},{"en":"Automatic posting discounts granted to entities purchasing goods or services","es":"Descuentos concedidos a compradores"}]},{"id":"t2q56","type":"drag","en":"You are implementing Business Central for a company.<br><br>The finance manager of the company must configure the system to post payments and expenses. The configuration must include the following capabilities:<ul><li>Get suggested payments to the external parties based on due dates and available funds.</li><li>Apply customer payments to multiple invoices.</li><li>Submit electronic payments to the bank.</li><li>Reimburse an employee to a dedicated bank account.</li></ul>You need to recommend the page the company should use for each requirement.<br><br>Which page should you recommend posting to for each requirement? To answer, move the appropriate pages to the correct requirements. You may use each page once, more than once, or not at all.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"El responsable financiero debe configurar el registro de pagos y gastos con estas capacidades:<ul><li>Obtener propuestas de pago a terceros según vencimientos y fondos disponibles.</li><li>Aplicar cobros de clientes a varias facturas.</li><li>Enviar pagos electrónicos al banco.</li><li>Reembolsar a un empleado en una cuenta bancaria específica.</li></ul>¿En qué página se registra cada requisito? Cada página puede usarse una vez, varias o ninguna.","src":"Topic 2 · Q56","valuesTitle":"Pages","targetHeader":["Requirement","Page"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Sales Journal","es":"Sales Journal (diario de ventas)"},{"id":"V2","en":"Payment Journal","es":"Payment Journal (diario de pagos)"},{"id":"V3","en":"Purchase Journal","es":"Purchase Journal (diario de compras)"},{"id":"V4","en":"Cash Receipt Journal","es":"Cash Receipt Journal (diario de cobros)"}],"targets":[{"en":"Suggested payments to external parties","es":"Propuestas de pago a terceros"},{"en":"Customer payments for multiple invoices","es":"Cobros de clientes para varias facturas"},{"en":"Electronic payments to bank","es":"Pagos electrónicos al banco"},{"en":"Dedicated bank account for employee reimbursement","es":"Reembolso a empleado en cuenta bancaria específica"}]},{"id":"t2q57","type":"drag","en":"You are implementing Dynamics 365 Business Central for a company. You set up the chart of accounts.<br><br>The finance manager must map general ledger accounts to posting groups to automate transaction posting.<br><br>You need to map entities to the general ledger accounts.<br><br>Which posting groups should you set up?","es":"Has configurado el plan de cuentas. El responsable financiero quiere asociar cuentas a grupos contables para automatizar los registros.<br><br>¿Qué grupo contable debes configurar para cada requisito?","src":"Topic 2 · Q57","valuesTitle":"Posting groups","targetHeader":["Requirement","Posting group"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Customer posting groups","es":"Customer posting groups"},{"id":"V2","en":"General business posting groups","es":"General business posting groups"},{"id":"V3","en":"General product posting groups","es":"General product posting groups"},{"id":"V4","en":"Tax/VAT business posting groups","es":"Tax/VAT business posting groups"},{"id":"V5","en":"Tax/VAT product posting groups","es":"Tax/VAT product posting groups"}],"targets":[{"en":"Specify who the company sells to and buys from.","es":"Indicar a quién vende y a quién compra la empresa."},{"en":"Specify the accounts to use for accounts receivable transactions.","es":"Indicar las cuentas de las operaciones de clientes (cuentas a cobrar)."},{"en":"Specify tax/VAT percentages and calculation types that apply to who the company sells to and buys from.","es":"Indicar porcentajes y tipos de cálculo de IVA según a quién se vende o compra."}]},{"id":"t2q58","type":"hotspot","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central. You are creating a general ledger (G/L) for a checking account in the chart of accounts.<br><br>You need to populate the fields on the G/L account card.<br><br>Which value should you select?","es":"Estás creando en el plan de cuentas una cuenta de mayor para una cuenta corriente bancaria.<br><br>¿Qué valor debes seleccionar en cada campo de la ficha?","src":"Topic 2 · Q58","rowsHeader":["Field","Value"],"rows":[{"en":"Income/Balance","es":"Income/Balance","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Income statement","es":"Income statement"},{"id":"b","en":"Balance sheet","es":"Balance sheet"}]},{"en":"Account Category","es":"Account Category","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Assets","es":"Assets"},{"id":"b","en":"Liabilities","es":"Liabilities"},{"id":"c","en":"Equity","es":"Equity"},{"id":"d","en":"Income","es":"Income"},{"id":"e","en":"Expense","es":"Expense"}]},{"en":"Account Type","es":"Account Type","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Posting","es":"Posting"},{"id":"b","en":"Heading","es":"Heading"},{"id":"c","en":"Begin-Total","es":"Begin-Total"},{"id":"d","en":"End-Total","es":"End-Total"}]},{"en":"Direct Posting","es":"Direct Posting","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Enabled","es":"Enabled"},{"id":"b","en":"Disabled","es":"Disabled"}]}]},{"id":"t2q59","type":"mr","en":"You are implementing Business Central for a company.<br><br>The accounting manager of the company must register inventory value and costs.<br><br>The accounting manager provides you with the chart of accounts.<br><br>You need to configure inventory posting for the company.<br><br>Which two posting groups should you use to register inventory value and costs? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.","es":"Implantas Business Central. El responsable de contabilidad debe registrar el valor y los costes del inventario y te entrega el plan de cuentas.<br><br>Debes configurar la contabilización del inventario. ¿Qué dos posting groups debes usar para registrar el valor y los costes del inventario?","src":"Topic 2 · Q59","options":[{"id":"A","en":"inventory posting groups","es":"inventory posting groups"},{"id":"B","en":"vendor posting groups","es":"vendor posting groups"},{"id":"C","en":"customer posting groups","es":"customer posting groups"},{"id":"D","en":"bank account posting groups","es":"bank account posting groups"},{"id":"E","en":"general product posting groups","es":"general product posting groups"}],"select":2},{"id":"t2q60","type":"mc","en":"A company has been using Dynamics 365 Business Central for many years.<br><br>A new accounting manager for the company reviews the chart of accounts. The manager wants to remove some general ledger accounts.<br><br>The Check G/L Account Usage field is selected in the General Ledger Setup.<br><br>You need to assist with the account deletions.<br><br>What is one requirement that enables deletion of a general ledger account?","es":"Una empresa lleva muchos años con Business Central. El nuevo responsable de contabilidad quiere eliminar algunas cuentas. En General Ledger Setup está marcado <b>Check G/L Account Usage</b>.<br><br>¿Qué requisito permite eliminar una cuenta del libro mayor?","src":"Topic 2 · Q60","options":[{"id":"A","en":"The account cannot be used in any account schedule.","es":"La cuenta no puede usarse en ningún account schedule."},{"id":"B","en":"The account cannot be used in any posting groups or posting setup.","es":"La cuenta no puede usarse en ningún posting group ni posting setup."},{"id":"C","en":"The general ledger account is configured to allow for deletion.","es":"La cuenta está configurada para permitir su eliminación."},{"id":"D","en":"The account must have ledger entries.","es":"La cuenta debe tener movimientos."}]},{"id":"t2q61","type":"hotspot","en":"A company is implementing Business Central.<br><br>The company must define its chart of accounts and financial statement report formats to match its old accounts and report formats.<br><br>You need to configure Business Central to produce comparable financial statements.<br><br>Which configuration should you use to complete each task?","es":"La empresa debe definir su plan de cuentas y el formato de sus estados financieros igual que los antiguos.<br><br>¿Qué configuración debes usar para cada tarea?","src":"Topic 2 · Q61","rowsHeader":["Task","Configuration"],"rows":[{"en":"Define the overall layout of financial statements.","es":"Definir la estructura general de los estados financieros.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"G/L account card","es":"G/L account card"},{"id":"b","en":"Indent subcategories","es":"Indent subcategories"},{"id":"c","en":"G/L Account Categories","es":"G/L Account Categories"},{"id":"d","en":"Generate financial reports","es":"Generate financial reports"}]},{"en":"Create category groups.","es":"Crear grupos de categorías.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"G/L account card","es":"G/L account card"},{"id":"b","en":"Indent subcategories","es":"Indent subcategories"},{"id":"c","en":"G/L Account Categories","es":"G/L Account Categories"},{"id":"d","en":"Generate financial reports","es":"Generate financial reports"}]},{"en":"Assign categories and subcategories.","es":"Asignar categorías y subcategorías.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"G/L account card","es":"G/L account card"},{"id":"b","en":"Indent subcategories","es":"Indent subcategories"},{"id":"c","en":"Move up or move down","es":"Move up or move down"},{"id":"d","en":"Generate financial reports","es":"Generate financial reports"}]},{"en":"Include new categories in your financial reports.","es":"Incluir las categorías nuevas en los informes financieros.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"G/L account card","es":"G/L account card"},{"id":"b","en":"Indent subcategories","es":"Indent subcategories"},{"id":"c","en":"G/L Account Categories","es":"G/L Account Categories"},{"id":"d","en":"Generate financial reports","es":"Generate financial reports"}]}]},{"id":"t2q62","type":"drag","en":"A company uses Business Central.<br><br>The finance manager requires the ability to delete zero balance general ledger (G/L) accounts.<br><br>You need to configure the system.<br><br>Which configuration should you use?","es":"El responsable financiero necesita poder eliminar cuentas de mayor con saldo cero.<br><br>¿Qué configuración debes usar para cada acción?","src":"Topic 2 · Q62","valuesTitle":"Configurations","targetHeader":["Action","Configuration"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Check G/L Account Usage","es":"Check G/L Account Usage"},{"id":"V2","en":"Check G/L Acc. Deletion After","es":"Check G/L Acc. Deletion After"},{"id":"V3","en":"Block Deletion of G/L Accounts","es":"Block Deletion of G/L Accounts"}],"targets":[{"en":"Set up rules to comply with local legislation.","es":"Definir reglas para cumplir la legislación local."},{"en":"Allow the deletion of G/L account with ledger entries.","es":"Permitir eliminar cuentas con movimientos."},{"en":"Block the deletion of G/L accounts in setup tables.","es":"Impedir eliminar cuentas usadas en tablas de configuración."}]},{"id":"t2q65","type":"mr","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The finance team must dispose a fixed asset.<br><br>You need to recommend the process to post the fixed asset disposal.<br><br>Which two actions should you recommend the company perform? Each correct answer presents a complete solution.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Finanzas debe dar de baja (disposal, enajenación) un activo fijo.<br><br>¿Qué dos acciones recomiendas? Cada respuesta correcta es una solución completa.","src":"Topic 2 · Q65","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Create and post a fixed asset G/L journal.","es":"Crear y registrar un fixed asset G/L journal."},{"id":"B","en":"Select a Tax Category when posting the sales invoice","es":"Seleccionar una Tax Category al registrar la factura de venta"},{"id":"C","en":"Create and post a sales invoice.","es":"Crear y registrar una factura de venta."},{"id":"D","en":"Manually adjust the depreciation amount in the fixed asset card.","es":"Ajustar a mano la amortización en la ficha del activo."},{"id":"E","en":"Use the Reverse Transactions function to cancel the fixed asset record.","es":"Usar Reverse Transactions para anular el activo."}],"select":2},{"id":"t2q66","type":"drag","en":"You are configuring Business Central for a client.<br><br>The client has the following requirements to process documents in the system:<ul><li>Invoice amounts in the local currency must never be rounded.</li><li>Details for general ledger (G/L) entries must be displayed in Preview Posting.</li><li>During data entry, users must receive an alert about issues in documents and journals to prevent users from posting.</li></ul>You need to configure General Ledger Setup options to complete the configuration.","es":"Un cliente necesita que:<ul><li>Los importes de factura en divisa local no se redondeen nunca.</li><li>Preview Posting muestre el detalle de los movimientos contables.</li><li>Al introducir datos, los usuarios reciban avisos de errores que impedirían registrar.</li></ul>¿Qué opción de General Ledger Setup corresponde a cada requisito?","src":"Topic 2 · Q66","valuesTitle":"Configuration options","targetHeader":["Requirement","Configuration option"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"LCY Code","es":"LCY Code"},{"id":"V2","en":"Enable Data Check","es":"Enable Data Check"},{"id":"V3","en":"Posting Preview Type","es":"Posting Preview Type"},{"id":"V4","en":"Inv. Rounding Precision (LCY)","es":"Inv. Rounding Precision (LCY)"}],"targets":[{"en":"Restrict rounding of invoice amounts in the local currency code.","es":"Limitar el redondeo de los importes de factura en divisa local."},{"en":"Enable display of details for G/L entries in Preview Posting.","es":"Mostrar el detalle de los movimientos en Preview Posting."},{"en":"Enable alerts about data issues while typing to prevent a user from posting.","es":"Avisar de errores mientras se escribe para evitar registros erróneos."}]},{"id":"t2q68","type":"mr","en":"A production company is implementing Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The company must be able to analyze the total acquisition and maintenance cost of each production line.<br><br>The production lines must be set up as main assets with all the machines on the line set up as components. Only the machines on the production line should have a book value and be depreciated.<br><br>You need to configure the system to post correctly for the production line assets.<br><br>Which two actions should you perform? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.","es":"Una empresa de producción implanta Business Central. Debe analizar el coste total de adquisición y mantenimiento de cada línea de producción.<br><br>Las líneas de producción se configuran como activos principales (main assets) y sus máquinas como componentes. Solo las máquinas deben tener valor contable y amortizarse.<br><br>¿Qué dos acciones debes realizar?","src":"Topic 2 · Q68","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Make the production line asset inactive.","es":"Marcar el activo de la línea de producción como inactivo."},{"id":"B","en":"Disable posting to main assets.","es":"Desactivar el registro en los activos principales."},{"id":"C","en":"Open the fixed asset card for the production line.","es":"Abrir la ficha del activo de la línea de producción."},{"id":"D","en":"Open the Fixed Asset Setup page.","es":"Abrir la página Fixed Asset Setup."}],"select":2},{"id":"t2q69","type":"mc","en":"A repair company is implementing Dynamics 365 Business Central. The company tracks its repair vehicles as fixed assets. Each vehicle has a salvage value that varies depending on the make and model.<br><br>The company requires the acquisition cost to be posted to the general ledger and the salvage value be included in the fixed asset ledger entries.<br><br>You need to post the salvage value.<br><br>What should you do?","es":"Una empresa de reparaciones implanta Business Central y controla sus vehículos como activos fijos. Cada vehículo tiene un valor residual (salvage value) que depende de la marca y el modelo.<br><br>El coste de adquisición debe registrarse en contabilidad y el valor residual debe incluirse en los movimientos del activo.<br><br>¿Qué debes hacer?","src":"Topic 2 · Q69","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Uses purchase invoice to post the acquisition cost and salvage value at the same time.","es":"Usar una factura de compra para registrar a la vez el coste de adquisición y el valor residual."},{"id":"B","en":"Use purchase order to post the acquisition cost and salvage value at the same time.","es":"Usar un pedido de compra para registrar a la vez el coste de adquisición y el valor residual."},{"id":"C","en":"Use a fixed asset journal to post the salvage value after the asset has been acquired","es":"Usar un fixed asset journal para registrar el valor residual después de adquirir el activo."},{"id":"D","en":"Enter the salvage value in the ending book value field in the depreciation book on the fixed asset card.","es":"Introducir el valor residual en el campo Ending Book Value del libro de amortización de la ficha."}]},{"id":"t2q71","type":"yn","en":"Note: This question is part of a series of questions that present the same scenario. Each question in the series contains a unique solution that might meet the stated goals. Some question sets might have more than one correct solution, while others might not have a correct solution.<br><br>A manufacturing company is using Dynamics 365 Business Central for fixed assets.<br><br>The company used a purchase order to acquire a new machine. The company received a separate invoice from a different vendor for the installation and delivery fees related to the purchase.<br><br>The company requires these acquisition costs to be added to the machine so that the total acquisition cost can be capitalized and then depreciated over the useful life of the asset.<br><br>You need to configure the solution.<br><br>Solution: Open the fixed asset G/L journal. Add the fixed asset number of the machine and choose appreciation for the fixed asset posting type. Add the sum of the installation and delivery fees to the Amount field. Insert the fixed asset balance account and post the journal.<br><br>Does the solution meet the goal?","es":"<i>Nota: esta pregunta forma parte de una serie con el mismo escenario. Cada pregunta propone una solución distinta que podría cumplir el objetivo.</i><br><br>Una empresa de fabricación usa Business Central para los activos fijos. Compró una máquina nueva con un pedido de compra y recibió aparte la factura de otro proveedor por la instalación y el transporte.<br><br>Esos costes deben añadirse a la máquina para capitalizar el coste total y amortizarlo durante su vida útil.<br><br><b>Solución:</b> abrir el fixed asset G/L journal, indicar el activo, elegir <b>Appreciation</b> como FA posting type, poner la suma de instalación y transporte en Amount, indicar la cuenta de contrapartida y registrar.<br><br>¿Cumple la solución el objetivo?","src":"Topic 2 · Q71","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Yes","es":"Sí"},{"id":"B","en":"No","es":"No"}]},{"id":"t2q72","type":"yn","en":"Note: This question is part of a series of questions that present the same scenario. (Mismo escenario que la #71.)<br><br>Solution: Open the fixed asset G/L journal. Add the fixed asset number of the machine and choose acquisition cost for the fixed asset posting type. Add the installation and delivery fee to the Amount field and insert the fixed asset balance account. Post the journal.<br><br>Does the solution meet the goal?","es":"<i>Nota: esta pregunta forma parte de una serie con el mismo escenario. Cada pregunta propone una solución distinta que podría cumplir el objetivo.</i><br><br>Una empresa de fabricación usa Business Central para los activos fijos. Compró una máquina nueva con un pedido de compra y recibió aparte la factura de otro proveedor por la instalación y el transporte.<br><br>Esos costes deben añadirse a la máquina para capitalizar el coste total y amortizarlo durante su vida útil.<br><br><b>Solución:</b> abrir el fixed asset G/L journal, indicar el activo, elegir <b>Acquisition Cost</b> como FA posting type, poner el importe de instalación y transporte, indicar la cuenta de contrapartida y registrar.<br><br>¿Cumple la solución el objetivo?","src":"Topic 2 · Q72","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Yes","es":"Sí"},{"id":"B","en":"No","es":"No"}]},{"id":"t2q73","type":"yn","en":"Note: This question is part of a series of questions that present the same scenario. (Mismo escenario que la #71.)<br><br>Solution: Cancel the acquisition cost posting for the machine by using the Cancel fixed asset entries batch job. Post a corrected acquisition entry with the total acquisition cost of the machine, installation, and delivery.<br><br>Does the solution meet the goal?","es":"<i>Nota: esta pregunta forma parte de una serie con el mismo escenario. Cada pregunta propone una solución distinta que podría cumplir el objetivo.</i><br><br>Una empresa de fabricación usa Business Central para los activos fijos. Compró una máquina nueva con un pedido de compra y recibió aparte la factura de otro proveedor por la instalación y el transporte.<br><br>Esos costes deben añadirse a la máquina para capitalizar el coste total y amortizarlo durante su vida útil.<br><br><b>Solución:</b> anular el registro de adquisición de la máquina con el proceso <b>Cancel FA Entries</b> y registrar una adquisición corregida con el coste total de máquina, instalación y transporte.<br><br>¿Cumple la solución el objetivo?","src":"Topic 2 · Q73","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Yes","es":"Sí"},{"id":"B","en":"No","es":"No"}]},{"id":"t2q74","type":"hotspot","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central to manage its financial and operational processes.<br><br>The company has the following configuration and document layout requirements:<ul><li>Ensure all branches use the same standardized invoice format.</li><li>Modify an existing sales invoice layout to include personalized payment terms.</li><li>Export a financial report to add pivot tables and graphs for refined data presentation.</li></ul>You need to implement the changes in Business Central.","es":"Una empresa necesita:<ul><li>Que todas las sucursales usen el mismo formato de factura.</li><li>Modificar un layout de factura de venta para incluir condiciones de pago personalizadas.</li><li>Exportar un informe financiero para añadir tablas dinámicas y gráficos.</li></ul>¿Qué configuración debes usar para cada requisito?","src":"Topic 2 · Q74","rowsHeader":["Requirement","Configuration"],"rows":[{"en":"Standardize the invoice format.","es":"Estandarizar el formato de factura.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Report Selection Sales","es":"Report Selection Sales"},{"id":"b","en":"Report Settings","es":"Report Settings"},{"id":"c","en":"RDLC layout","es":"RDLC layout"},{"id":"d","en":"Word layout","es":"Word layout"}]},{"en":"Modify an existing sales invoice layout.","es":"Modificar un layout de factura de venta existente.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Report Layout Selection","es":"Report Layout Selection"},{"id":"b","en":"Report Settings","es":"Report Settings"},{"id":"c","en":"Printer Management","es":"Printer Management"},{"id":"d","en":"Document Layouts","es":"Document Layouts"}]},{"en":"Export a financial report with refined data presentation.","es":"Exportar un informe financiero con una presentación elaborada.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Excel layouts","es":"Excel layouts"},{"id":"b","en":"RDLC report","es":"RDLC report"},{"id":"c","en":"Document Layouts","es":"Document Layouts"},{"id":"d","en":"Report Settings","es":"Report Settings"}]}]},{"id":"t2q76","type":"yn","en":"Note: This question is part of a series of questions that present the same scenario. Each question in the series contains a unique solution that might meet the stated goals. Some question sets might have more than one correct solution, while others might not have a correct solution.<br><br>A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central to track and manage fixed assets.<br><br>The company must ensure that depreciation entries for newly acquired fixed assets are automatically recorded in two different depreciation books at the same time.<br><br>You need to configure the fixed asset setup.<br><br>Solution: Select a duplication depreciation book in the Fixed Asset G/L Journal.<br><br>Does the solution meet the goal?","es":"<i>Nota: esta pregunta forma parte de una serie con el mismo escenario. Cada pregunta propone una solución distinta que podría cumplir el objetivo.</i><br><br>Una empresa usa Business Central para controlar sus activos fijos. Las amortizaciones de los activos nuevos deben registrarse automáticamente a la vez en dos libros de amortización (depreciation books).<br><br>Debes configurar los activos fijos.<br><br><b>Solución:</b> seleccionar un libro de duplicación (duplication depreciation book) en el Fixed Asset G/L Journal.<br><br>¿Cumple la solución el objetivo?","src":"Topic 2 · Q76","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Yes","es":"Sí"},{"id":"B","en":"No","es":"No"}]},{"id":"t2q77","type":"yn","en":"Note: This question is part of a series of questions that present the same scenario. (Mismo escenario que la #76.)<br><br>Solution: Update the FA Posting Type setup.<br><br>Does the solution meet the goal?","es":"<i>Nota: esta pregunta forma parte de una serie con el mismo escenario. Cada pregunta propone una solución distinta que podría cumplir el objetivo.</i><br><br>Una empresa usa Business Central para controlar sus activos fijos. Las amortizaciones de los activos nuevos deben registrarse automáticamente a la vez en dos libros de amortización (depreciation books).<br><br>Debes configurar los activos fijos.<br><br><b>Solución:</b> actualizar la configuración de FA Posting Type.<br><br>¿Cumple la solución el objetivo?","src":"Topic 2 · Q77","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Yes","es":"Sí"},{"id":"B","en":"No","es":"No"}]},{"id":"t2q78","type":"yn","en":"Note: This question is part of a series of questions that present the same scenario. (Mismo escenario que la #76.)<br><br>Solution: Enable a duplication list to post to multiple depreciation books.<br><br>Does the solution meet the goal?","es":"<i>Nota: esta pregunta forma parte de una serie con el mismo escenario. Cada pregunta propone una solución distinta que podría cumplir el objetivo.</i><br><br>Una empresa usa Business Central para controlar sus activos fijos. Las amortizaciones de los activos nuevos deben registrarse automáticamente a la vez en dos libros de amortización (depreciation books).<br><br>Debes configurar los activos fijos.<br><br><b>Solución:</b> activar una lista de duplicación para registrar en varios libros de amortización.<br><br>¿Cumple la solución el objetivo?","src":"Topic 2 · Q78","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Yes","es":"Sí"},{"id":"B","en":"No","es":"No"}]},{"id":"t2q79","type":"drag","en":"A company is setting up fixed asset tracking in Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The finance team must be able to track fixed assets in the following ways:<ul><li>Categorize assets to separate tangible and intangible items.</li><li>Group physical assets into specific categories based on their type or usage.</li><li>Track the storage of each asset.</li></ul>You need to configure the fixed asset tracking.<br><br>Which classification type should you use? To answer, move the appropriate classification types to the correct business requirements. You may use each classification type once, more than once, or not at all.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Una empresa configura el seguimiento de fixed assets (activos fijos). Finanzas necesita:<ul><li>Clasificar los activos para separar tangibles e intangibles.</li><li>Agrupar los activos físicos en categorías según su tipo o uso.</li><li>Saber dónde está cada activo.</li></ul>¿Qué tipo de clasificación debes usar para cada requisito? Cada tipo puede usarse una vez, varias o ninguna.","src":"Topic 2 · Q79","valuesTitle":"Classification types","targetHeader":["Business requirement","Classification type"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Fixed Asset Class","es":"Fixed Asset Class (clase)"},{"id":"V2","en":"Fixed Asset Subclass","es":"Fixed Asset Subclass (subclase)"},{"id":"V3","en":"Fixed Asset Location","es":"Fixed Asset Location (ubicación)"},{"id":"V4","en":"Fixed Asset Posting Group","es":"Fixed Asset Posting Group (grupo contable)"}],"targets":[{"en":"Categorize assets to separate tangible and intangible items.","es":"Clasificar los activos para separar tangibles e intangibles."},{"en":"Group physical items into categories.","es":"Agrupar los activos físicos en categorías."},{"en":"Record the physical place of assets.","es":"Registrar el lugar físico de los activos."}]},{"id":"t2q80","type":"yn","en":"<b>Note: This question is part of a series of questions that present the same scenario. Each question in the series contains a unique solution that might meet the stated goals. Some question sets might have more than one correct solution, while others might not have a correct solution.</b><br><br>A manufacturing company is using Dynamics 365 Business Central for fixed assets.<br><br>The company used a purchase order to acquire a new machine. The company received a separate invoice from a different vendor for the installation and delivery fees related to the purchase.<br><br>The company requires these acquisition costs to be added to the machine so that the total acquisition cost can be capitalized and then depreciated over the useful life of the asset.<br><br>You need to configure the solution.<br><br>Solution: Create a purchase invoice for the installation and delivery fees. Add the fixed asset number of the machine to the invoice lines and post the invoice.<br><br>Does the solution meet the goal?","es":"<b>Nota: esta pregunta forma parte de una serie con el mismo escenario. Cada pregunta propone una solución distinta que podría cumplir el objetivo. Algunas series tienen más de una solución correcta y otras ninguna.</b><br><br>Una empresa compró una máquina con un pedido de compra y recibe de otro proveedor una factura aparte por instalación y transporte. Estos costes deben sumarse a la máquina para capitalizar el coste total de adquisición y amortizarlo.<br><br>Solución: crear una factura de compra por la instalación y el transporte, poner en las líneas el número de activo fijo de la máquina y registrarla.<br><br>¿La solución cumple el objetivo?","src":"Topic 2 · Q80","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Yes","es":"Sí"},{"id":"B","en":"No","es":"No"}]},{"id":"t2q81","type":"yn","en":"Note: This question is part of a series of questions that present the same scenario. (Mismo escenario que la #76.)<br><br>Solution: Run the create FA depreciation books batch job.<br><br>Does the solution meet the goal?","es":"<i>Nota: esta pregunta forma parte de una serie con el mismo escenario. Cada pregunta propone una solución distinta que podría cumplir el objetivo.</i><br><br>Una empresa usa Business Central para controlar sus activos fijos. Las amortizaciones de los activos nuevos deben registrarse automáticamente a la vez en dos libros de amortización (depreciation books).<br><br>Debes configurar los activos fijos.<br><br><b>Solución:</b> ejecutar el proceso <b>Create FA Depreciation Books</b>.<br><br>¿Cumple la solución el objetivo?","src":"Topic 2 · Q81","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Yes","es":"Sí"},{"id":"B","en":"No","es":"No"}]},{"id":"s2q15","type":"build","en":"An accountant discovers inconsistencies between financial statements and balances in the chart of accounts.<br><br>You suspect that the discrepancies might be a result of missing categories and subcategories.<br><br>You need to ensure that the financial statements match the chart of accounts.<br><br>Which three actions should you perform in sequence?","es":"Un contable detecta diferencias entre los estados financieros y los saldos del plan de cuentas. Sospechas que faltan categorías y subcategorías.<br><br>¿Qué tres acciones debes realizar y en qué orden?","src":"Secuencial Topic 2 · Q15","slots":3,"actions":[{"id":"A","en":"Create subcategories for each category.","es":"Crear subcategorías para cada categoría."},{"id":"B","en":"Rename the general ledger account to match the category and subcategory in the chart of accounts.","es":"Renombrar la cuenta para que coincida con la categoría y subcategoría."},{"id":"C","en":"Verify that the financial statements match the chart of accounts.","es":"Verificar que los estados financieros coinciden con el plan de cuentas."},{"id":"D","en":"Add the accounts to the analysis view.","es":"Añadir las cuentas a la analysis view."},{"id":"E","en":"Add the missing categories and subcategories to the general ledger accounts.","es":"Asignar las categorías y subcategorías que faltan a las cuentas."}]},{"id":"s2q34","type":"build","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>You need to configure the system to meet the following requirements for a purchasing agent:<ul><li>Create and post purchase documents including purchase receipt lines.</li><li>Do not allow agents to read general ledger (G/L) or bank balances.</li><li>Restrict access to view G/L amounts.</li><li>Ensure that purchasing agents can select G/L codes on purchase documents.</li></ul>You need to restrict access to view G/L amounts.<br><br>Which three actions should you perform in sequence?","es":"Un agente de compras debe crear y registrar documentos de compra y elegir cuentas de mayor en ellos, pero no ver saldos contables ni bancarios.<br><br>Debes restringir la visualización de importes contables. ¿Qué tres acciones debes realizar y en qué orden?","src":"Secuencial Topic 2 · Q34","slots":3,"actions":[{"id":"A","en":"Select the permissions sets that you want to modify.","es":"Seleccionar los permission sets a modificar."},{"id":"B","en":"Remove page permissions for the G/L account list page.","es":"Quitar permisos de página a la lista de cuentas."},{"id":"C","en":"Remove page permissions for chart of accounts, G/L entries and G/L account card.","es":"Quitar permisos de página al plan de cuentas, movimientos y ficha de cuenta."},{"id":"D","en":"In the Field Filter column, set the value to 1500.","es":"En la columna Field Filter, poner el valor 1500."},{"id":"E","en":"Assign a permission set to a user.","es":"Asignar un permission set a un usuario."},{"id":"F","en":"In the row for the G/L account table, select the Security Filter column.","es":"En la fila de la tabla G/L Account, seleccionar la columna Security Filter."}]},{"id":"s2q38","type":"build","en":"You set up a new company for a customer.<br><br>The customer requires that two global dimensions be automatically checked at transaction when income statement accounts are used.<br><br>You need to set up the requirements for all income statement accounts at once.<br><br>Which four actions should you perform in sequence? To answer, move the appropriate actions from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.","es":"Configuras una company nueva. El cliente exige que, al usar cuentas de la cuenta de resultados (income statement), se compruebe automáticamente que llevan las dos global dimensions (dimensiones globales).<br><br>Debes configurarlo para todas las cuentas de resultados a la vez. ¿Qué cuatro acciones debes realizar y en qué orden?","src":"Secuencial Topic 2 · Q38","slots":4,"actions":[{"id":"A","en":"Navigate to Account and select <b>Dimensions-Single</b>.","es":"Ir a Account y seleccionar <b>Dimensions-Single</b>."},{"id":"B","en":"Set up the Dimension Value Code in General Ledger Setup.","es":"Configurar el Dimension Value Code en General Ledger Setup."},{"id":"C","en":"Navigate to Account and select <b>Dimensions-Multiple</b>.","es":"Ir a Account y seleccionar <b>Dimensions-Multiple</b>."},{"id":"D","en":"Define the dimension code and change Value Posting to Code Mandatory.","es":"Definir el código de dimensión y cambiar Value Posting a Code Mandatory."},{"id":"E","en":"Navigate to Chart of Accounts and select the <b>Filter</b> option in the Income/Balance column.","es":"Ir a Chart of Accounts y usar <b>Filter</b> en la columna Income/Balance."},{"id":"F","en":"Select all income statement accounts.","es":"Seleccionar todas las cuentas de resultados."}]},{"id":"s2q43","type":"build","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The company plans to automatically create vendor payments based on posted purchase invoices. The payments should be summarized based on the vendor invoices.<br><br>You need to configure the vendor payments.<br><br>Which three actions should you perform in sequence?","es":"La empresa quiere crear automáticamente los pagos a proveedores a partir de las facturas registradas, resumidos por proveedor.<br><br>¿Qué tres acciones debes realizar y en qué orden?","src":"Secuencial Topic 2 · Q43","slots":3,"actions":[{"id":"A","en":"On the Prepare tab, select Suggest Vendor Payments.","es":"En la pestaña Prepare, seleccionar Suggest Vendor Payments."},{"id":"B","en":"On the Options page, enter the last payment date and disable the Summarize per Vendor option.","es":"En Options, indicar la última fecha de pago y desactivar Summarize per Vendor."},{"id":"C","en":"Navigate to General Journals.","es":"Ir a General Journals."},{"id":"D","en":"On the Related tab, open the Payments menu and select Print Remittance Advice.","es":"En Related > Payments, seleccionar Print Remittance Advice."},{"id":"E","en":"Navigate to Payment Journals.","es":"Ir a Payment Journals."},{"id":"F","en":"On the Prepare tab, select Suggest Employee Payments.","es":"En la pestaña Prepare, seleccionar Suggest Employee Payments."},{"id":"G","en":"On the Options page, enter the posting date and enable the Summarize per Vendor option.","es":"En Options, indicar la fecha de registro y activar Summarize per Vendor."}]},{"id":"s2q48","type":"build","en":"A company uses Business Central.<br><br>The operations team posts an incorrect quantity received on a purchase order.<br><br>You need to undo the quantity posting on the posted purchase receipt before the purchase order is invoiced.<br><br>Which four actions should you perform in sequence?","es":"El equipo de operaciones ha registrado mal la cantidad recibida de un pedido de compra.<br><br>Debes deshacer la recepción registrada antes de facturar. ¿Qué cuatro acciones debes realizar y en qué orden?","src":"Secuencial Topic 2 · Q48","slots":4,"actions":[{"id":"A","en":"Navigate to the Posted Purchase Receipts page.","es":"Ir a Posted Purchase Receipts."},{"id":"B","en":"Select Yes in the confirmation pop-up box.","es":"Pulsar Yes en la confirmación."},{"id":"C","en":"In Lines, select the line or lines that you want to undo, select the Function button, and select the Undo Receipt action.","es":"En Lines, seleccionar las líneas y la acción Undo Receipt."},{"id":"D","en":"On the Posted Purchase Receipts page, select the Find Entries action.","es":"En Posted Purchase Receipts, seleccionar Find Entries."},{"id":"E","en":"In Lines, select the Function button, and select the Order Tracking action.","es":"En Lines, seleccionar Order Tracking."},{"id":"F","en":"Open the posted purchase receipt that you want to undo.","es":"Abrir la recepción registrada a deshacer."}]},{"id":"s2q63","type":"build","en":"A company is implementing Business Central.<br><br>The finance manager must be able to streamline the process of recording customer payments.<br><br>You need to recommend a quick and easy method to process customer payments from the Customer Registration page.<br><br>Which four actions should you perform in sequence?","es":"El responsable financiero quiere agilizar el registro de cobros de clientes desde la página de registro de pagos.<br><br>¿Qué cuatro acciones debes realizar y en qué orden?","src":"Secuencial Topic 2 · Q63","slots":4,"actions":[{"id":"A","en":"Open the Register Customer Payments page from the Customer List page.","es":"Abrir Register Customer Payments desde la lista de clientes."},{"id":"B","en":"Confirm bank account information.","es":"Confirmar los datos de la cuenta bancaria."},{"id":"C","en":"Access the cash receipt journals to review or process payments.","es":"Ir a los diarios de cobros para revisar o procesar los pagos."},{"id":"D","en":"Mark each invoice as paid","es":"Marcar cada factura como pagada."},{"id":"E","en":"Adjust amounts if required.","es":"Ajustar importes si es necesario."},{"id":"F","en":"Post payments.","es":"Registrar los pagos."}]},{"id":"s2q64","type":"build","en":"A company uses Business Central.<br><br>A user mistakenly partly applied two cash receipts to a posted sales transaction.<br><br>You need to remove the first cash receipt from the posted sales transaction to correct the mistake.<br><br>Which four actions should you perform in sequence?","es":"Un usuario ha aplicado parcialmente, por error, dos cobros a una venta registrada.<br><br>Debes quitar el primer cobro. ¿Qué cuatro acciones debes realizar y en qué orden?","src":"Secuencial Topic 2 · Q64","slots":4,"actions":[{"id":"A","en":"Post a reversing cash receipt and select the customer and relevant payment entry.","es":"Registrar un cobro inverso seleccionando el cliente y el pago."},{"id":"B","en":"Apply the second payment to the customer ledger entry.","es":"Aplicar el segundo pago al movimiento del cliente."},{"id":"C","en":"Navigate to Reverse Transaction from the relevant detailed customer ledger entry.","es":"Ir a Reverse Transaction desde el movimiento detallado."},{"id":"D","en":"Unapply the first payment.","es":"Desaplicar el primer pago."},{"id":"E","en":"Unapply the second payment.","es":"Desaplicar el segundo pago."},{"id":"F","en":"Navigate to Unapply Entries from the relevant customer ledger entry.","es":"Ir a Unapply Entries desde el movimiento del cliente."}]},{"id":"s2q67","type":"build","en":"A manufacturing company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central. The company implemented fixed assets by using a straight-line depreciation method for its financials.<br><br>The company plans to use a different method to track tax depreciation in Business Central. The company already created and configured the tax depreciation book with the code Tax.<br><br>You need to configure existing fixed assets to use multiple depreciation books.<br><br>Which four actions should you perform in sequence?","es":"Una empresa amortiza sus activos fijos por el método lineal y quiere otro método para la amortización fiscal. Ya existe el libro de amortización fiscal <b>Tax</b>.<br><br>Debes configurar los activos existentes con varios libros. ¿Qué cuatro acciones debes realizar y en qué orden?","src":"Secuencial Topic 2 · Q67","slots":4,"actions":[{"id":"A","en":"Open the depreciation book card.","es":"Abrir la ficha del libro de amortización."},{"id":"B","en":"Open the fixed asset card.","es":"Abrir la ficha del activo fijo."},{"id":"C","en":"Add the depreciation method of straight-line and fill in the remaining fields.","es":"Añadir el método lineal y completar los demás campos."},{"id":"D","en":"Select the Add more depreciation books link.","es":"Seleccionar el enlace Add more depreciation books."},{"id":"E","en":"Add a new line and select the tax depreciation book code.","es":"Añadir una línea y elegir el libro fiscal."},{"id":"F","en":"Add a depreciation method of declining balance 1 and fill in the remaining fields.","es":"Añadir el método Declining-Balance 1 y completar los demás campos."}]},{"id":"s2q70","type":"build","en":"A manufacturing company is implementing Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The company has production machines that consist of several parts. The company requires the parts to be grouped together with a main asset in the fixed asset module.<br><br>You need to set up a component list for the main asset.<br><br>Which four actions should you perform in sequence?","es":"Una empresa tiene máquinas formadas por varias piezas, que deben agruparse con un activo principal.<br><br>Debes crear la lista de componentes del activo principal. ¿Qué cuatro acciones debes realizar y en qué orden?","src":"Secuencial Topic 2 · Q70","slots":4,"actions":[{"id":"A","en":"Open the fixed asset card for the main asset","es":"Abrir la ficha del activo principal."},{"id":"B","en":"Choose the main asset components action","es":"Elegir la acción Main Asset Components."},{"id":"C","en":"Choose the fixed asset numbers of the assets you want to add as components.","es":"Elegir los números de los activos que serán componentes."},{"id":"D","en":"Open the fixed asset card for the component asset.","es":"Abrir la ficha del activo componente."},{"id":"E","en":"Set up the main asset and all its components as individual fixed assets.","es":"Crear el activo principal y sus componentes como activos fijos individuales."}]},{"id":"s2q75","type":"build","en":"A delivery company is implementing Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The company has the following requirements:<ul><li>Track fixed assets in the system.</li><li>Require purchase orders to be issued to vendors to purchase new delivery trucks. The fixed asset card will be created by the accounting department prior to the purchase of the asset.</li></ul>You need to demonstrate how the procurement department can use a purchase order to acquire a delivery truck as a fixed asset.<br><br>Which five actions should you perform in sequence?","es":"Una empresa de reparto quiere controlar sus activos fijos y comprar los camiones mediante pedidos de compra. Contabilidad crea antes la ficha del activo.<br><br>Debes mostrar cómo adquirir un camión como activo fijo con un pedido de compra. ¿Qué cinco acciones debes realizar y en qué orden?","src":"Secuencial Topic 2 · Q75","slots":5,"actions":[{"id":"A","en":"Create a new purchase order for the delivery truck vendor.","es":"Crear un pedido de compra al proveedor del camión."},{"id":"B","en":"Post receipt and invoice.","es":"Registrar la recepción y la factura."},{"id":"C","en":"In the lines, select a line type of fixed asset.","es":"En las líneas, elegir el tipo Fixed Asset."},{"id":"D","en":"Choose the Acquire action on the fixed asset card.","es":"Elegir la acción Acquire en la ficha del activo."},{"id":"E","en":"In the lines, select a line type of item.","es":"En las líneas, elegir el tipo Item."},{"id":"F","en":"Add quantity and cost.","es":"Indicar cantidad y coste."},{"id":"G","en":"In the Number field, add the fixed asset number.","es":"En el campo No., indicar el número del activo fijo."},{"id":"H","en":"In the Number field, add the item number.","es":"En el campo No., indicar el número del artículo."}]},{"id":"cs1t2q44","type":"mc","en":"You need to resolve the issue reported by the AR users from the finance department.<br>What should you do?","es":"Debes resolver el problema que indican los usuarios de cuentas a cobrar (AR) del departamento financiero.<br><br>¿Qué debes hacer?","src":"Case Study 1 · Topic 2 · Q44","case":"CS1","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Switch Blocked on the Customer Card to Yes.","es":"Poner Blocked = Yes en la ficha del cliente."},{"id":"B","en":"Switch Direct Posting on the G/L Account Card to No.","es":"Poner Direct Posting = No en la ficha de la cuenta contable."},{"id":"C","en":"Switch Blocked on the G/L Account Card to Yes.","es":"Poner Blocked = Yes en la ficha de la cuenta contable."},{"id":"D","en":"Switch Direct Posting on the G/L Account Card to Yes.","es":"Poner Direct Posting = Yes en la ficha de la cuenta contable."}]},{"id":"cs1t2q45","type":"mr","en":"You need to train the Accounts Receivable (AR) department how to correct customer payment application issues.<br>What are two possible ways to achieve this? Each correct answer presents a complete solution.","es":"Debes formar al departamento de cuentas a cobrar (AR) en cómo corregir errores al aplicar pagos de clientes.<br><br>¿Cuáles son dos formas posibles de hacerlo?","src":"Case Study 1 · Topic 2 · Q45","case":"CS1","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Unapply entries from the customer ledger entries.","es":"Desaplicar desde los movimientos de cliente (customer ledger entries)."},{"id":"B","en":"Unapply entries from the detailed customer ledger entries.","es":"Desaplicar desde los movimientos detallados de cliente (detailed customer ledger entries)."},{"id":"C","en":"Unapply entries from the customer card.","es":"Desaplicar desde la ficha del cliente."},{"id":"D","en":"Apply entries from the Detailed Customer Ledger Entries page.","es":"Aplicar movimientos desde la página Detailed Customer Ledger Entries."}],"select":2},{"id":"cs1t2q46","type":"mc","en":"You need to configure Business Central to display G/L entries as required by the accounting team.<br>Which configuration should you use?","es":"Debes configurar Business Central para mostrar los movimientos contables (G/L entries) como necesita el equipo de contabilidad.<br><br>¿Qué configuración debes usar?","src":"Case Study 1 · Topic 2 · Q46","case":"CS1","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Show Amounts","es":"Show Amounts"},{"id":"B","en":"Check G/L Account Usage","es":"Check G/L Account Usage"},{"id":"C","en":"G/L Account Card","es":"G/L Account Card"},{"id":"D","en":"Debit/Credit","es":"Debit/Credit"}]},{"id":"cs1t2q49","type":"hotspot","en":"You need to create accounting periods based on the requirements from the finance department.<br>Which values should you use for each configuration?","es":"Debes crear los periodos contables según los requisitos del departamento financiero.<br><br>¿Qué valor debes usar en cada configuración?","src":"Case Study 1 · Topic 2 · Q49","case":"CS1","rowsHeader":["Configuration","Value"],"rows":[{"en":"Starting date","es":"Starting date","options":[{"id":"a","en":"01/01/YYYY","es":"01/01/YYYY"},{"id":"b","en":"06/30/YYYY","es":"06/30/YYYY"},{"id":"c","en":"07/01/YYYY","es":"07/01/YYYY"}]},{"en":"No. of periods","es":"No. of periods","options":[{"id":"a","en":"4","es":"4"},{"id":"b","en":"12","es":"12"},{"id":"c","en":"13","es":"13"}]},{"en":"Period length","es":"Period length","options":[{"id":"a","en":"1M","es":"1M"},{"id":"b","en":"1Q","es":"1Q"},{"id":"c","en":"1Y","es":"1Y"}]}]},{"id":"cs2t2q54","type":"mr","en":"You need to configure the system to post to the receivables account for wholesale customers.<br>Which two configurations should you use? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.","es":"Debes configurar el sistema para registrar en la cuenta de clientes (receivables) de los clientes mayoristas (wholesale).<br><br>¿Qué dos configuraciones debes usar?","src":"Case Study 2 · Topic 2 · Q54","case":"CS2","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Receivables account 13100","es":"Receivables account 13100"},{"id":"B","en":"General Posting Setup","es":"General Posting Setup"},{"id":"C","en":"Receivables account 13200","es":"Receivables account 13200"},{"id":"D","en":"General Business Posting Groups","es":"General Business Posting Groups"},{"id":"E","en":"Customer Posting Groups","es":"Customer Posting Groups"}],"select":2},{"id":"cs2t2q55","type":"hotspot","en":"You need to select the values for the customer payment terms.<br>Which values should you use?","es":"Debes elegir los valores de los términos de pago de los clientes.<br><br>¿Qué valores debes usar?","src":"Case Study 2 · Topic 2 · Q55","case":"CS2","rowsHeader":["Customer payment term","Value"],"rows":[{"en":"Discount % for wholesale customer payment term","es":"Discount % del término de pago mayorista","options":[{"id":"a","en":"2","es":"2"},{"id":"b","en":"10","es":"10"},{"id":"c","en":"15","es":"15"},{"id":"d","en":"25","es":"25"}]},{"en":"Due Date Calculation for retail customer payment term","es":"Due Date Calculation del término de pago minorista","options":[{"id":"a","en":"0D","es":"0D"},{"id":"b","en":"10D","es":"10D"},{"id":"c","en":"15D","es":"15D"},{"id":"d","en":"30D","es":"30D"}]},{"en":"Discount Date Calculation for wholesale customer payment term","es":"Discount Date Calculation del término de pago mayorista","options":[{"id":"a","en":"0D","es":"0D"},{"id":"b","en":"10D","es":"10D"},{"id":"c","en":"15D","es":"15D"},{"id":"d","en":"30D","es":"30D"}]},{"en":"Due Date Calculation for wholesale customer payment term","es":"Due Date Calculation del término de pago mayorista","options":[{"id":"a","en":"0D","es":"0D"},{"id":"b","en":"10D","es":"10D"},{"id":"c","en":"15D","es":"15D"},{"id":"d","en":"30D","es":"30D"}]}]}]};
